<node id="&quot;WALL STREET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wall Street is a term used to describe the financial district of New York City, known for its major stock exchanges and financial institutions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wall Street is mentioned as a financial hub where big tech stocks influenced market movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wall Street is mentioned as the place where stock market activities happened, indicating its geographical and financial significance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wall Street refers to the financial markets in the United States, particularly significant as the rally that benefits the ASX is partly attributed to its performance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wall Street's September slump is mentioned as a negative influence on the global markets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wall Street is mentioned as a place where the S&amp;P 500 and Dow Jones fell, implying it is a financial hub and a location of significant economic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wall Street refers to the financial markets that are benchmarks for the US economy's performance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wall Street represents the financial sector that appears to be reacting to events in the crypto market."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wall Street is mentioned as a global financial hub where big tech companies like Microsoft and Alphabet report their results, influencing the market."</data>
