  <data key="d0">"INDEX"</data>
  <data key="d1">"S&amp;P 500 is a stock market index that measures the stock performance of 500 large companies listed on stock exchanges in the U.S., mentioned as having climbed points."&lt;SEP&gt;"S&amp;P 500 is a stock market index tracking the performance of 500 large companies listed on stock exchanges in the U.S., relevant for gauging the overall health of the stock market and economy."&lt;SEP&gt;"S&amp;P 500's significant losses are noted as part of a broader market trend."&lt;SEP&gt;"The S&amp;P 500 is a stock market index that fell 0.7 per cent on the day, ending a four-day winning streak."&lt;SEP&gt;"S&amp;P 500 represents a key performance indicator for the U.S. stock market, showing a decline on that day."&lt;SEP&gt;"The S&amp;P 500 is a major stock market index mentioned as having dropped due to rising treasury yields."</data>
