<node id="&quot;INFLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Inflation affects purchasing power and cost structures, influencing the organizations' profitability and stock performance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation is an economic measure directly impacted by interest rates and job market data, affecting overall economic health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation is mentioned as a concern affecting consumer confidence and spending patterns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation refers to the rate at which the general level of prices for goods and services is rising, and, subsequently, purchasing power is falling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation is mentioned as having decreased from its peak, which is a significant economic concept affecting monetary policy and market confidence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation, particularly consumer-level inflation, is an economic indicator that influences the Federal Reserve's monetary policy decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation is referenced as the economic condition that the Federal Reserve is attempting to combat through aggressive interest rate hikes, which in turn affect the housing market and mortgage rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation, especially affecting young workers, is an economic concept that has contributed to the financial stress and cynicism among Gen Z towards saving."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation refers to the increase in prices and the decrease in purchasing power, which has already led consumers to pull back on spending in Nike's key product sectors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation refers to the general increase in prices and living costs, which can be exacerbated by climate change impacts and policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation is mentioned as an independent factor affecting the national budget and economic projections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation is addressed as a pressing problem in the State of the Nation Address, indicating its impact on the economy and welfare."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation is highlighted as the country's most pressing issue, with an occurrence rate of 6.6% above the target range set by the BSP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation is mentioned as a factor contributing to the rising cost of concert tickets, adding to the challenges fans face in accessing live events."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation is a key economic concept being managed by the Federal Reserve through aggressive interest rate policies, which in turn affect the housing market and mortgage rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation is an economic event characterized by a general increase in prices and fall in the purchasing value of money, which is the focal point of the central banks' policy-making debate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflation is the rate at which the general level of prices for goods and services is rising, and subsequently, purchasing power is falling, often targeted by central banks through monetary policy."</data>
