<node id="&quot;FTX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"FTX is a crypto trading firm at the center of the trial, representing the business SBF co-founded."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the collapsed crypto exchange at the center of the legal proceedings, linked to allegations of fraud and money laundering."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the company at the center of the trial, facing serious charges related to its collapse."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the crypto exchange that faced a significant collapse, leading to bankruptcy and a criminal trial for its former CEO, Sam Bankman-Fried."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is a cryptocurrency exchange that collapsed due to financial discrepancies and is associated with SBF's controversial actions and management style."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the crypto exchange founded and led by SBF, the focal point of the financial fraud case and the subject of Lewis's book and media interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the cryptocurrency exchange, owned by Sam Bankman-Fried, that is at the center of the legal trial over alleged fraudulent activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is a cryptocurrency exchange and trading platform, central to the events described in the text, including its risk management practices and growth challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the cryptocurrency exchange founded by Sam Bankman-Fried, which eventually failed due to misappropriation of customer funds and other issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is a cryptocurrency exchange that is facing legal issues due to alleged misappropriation of customer funds and mismanagement of its accounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is involved in borrowing customer funds and establishing a venture fund, suggesting its role in the financial and strategic planning of related entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the failed cryptocurrency exchange founded by Bankman-Fried, which is the subject of a criminal trial for its collapse due to financial mismanagement."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the primary company involved in Alameda's controversial financial dealings and was publicly distanced while maintaining close private ties with Alameda Research."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the cryptocurrency exchange at the center of the trial, involved in a massive scam."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the cryptocurrency exchange company founded by Gabe Bankman-Fried, associated with major financial irregularities and regulatory scrutiny."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is described as a cryptocurrency exchange where a customer's money becomes inaccessible, leading to a cross-examination issue."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the crypto exchange CEOed by Sam Bankman-Fried, which underwent financial turmoil during the mentioned period, lacking a chief risk officer which became an issue during the crisis."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX was a cryptocurrency exchange, which is central to the trial, facing allegations of fraud and mismanagement of customer funds."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the bankrupt cryptocurrency exchange at the center of the trial, involved in financial crimes and collapse."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the cryptocurrency empire that failed, leading to the fraud charges against its former co-founder, Yedidia."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX was a cryptocurrency exchange, central to the case against its CEO, Sam Bankman-Fried, on charges of fraud and conspiracy."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the central organization around which the document revolves, discussing its bankruptcy and customer funds issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the company under investigation for customer and investor fraud, discussed in the context of the jury's confusion about its internal decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is the primary organization at the center of the financial crisis and legal scrutiny mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is a former competitor to Coinbase that collapsed under scandal and is associated with Sam Bankman-Fried's downfall."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX is a previously prominent crypto trading platform that failed, affecting market dynamics and investor confidence."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTX, once a competitor of Binance, is mentioned in connection with Binance's CEO's controversial comments that are implied to have contributed to its collapse."</data>
