<node id="&quot;ALAMEDA RESEARCH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Alameda Research is a co-founded crypto-trading firm by Sam Bankman-Fried, associated with FTX and involved in the financial fraud investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is a crypto trading firm that allegedly received funding from FTX customer transactions and was used by SBF for various purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is a former entity under SBF's direction, associated with the use of customer funds for repayment and investment activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is a crypto hedge fund owned by Sam Bankman-Fried, mentioned as part of the prosecution's allegations against Bankman-Fried."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is a sister company to SBF and a trader on its platform, mentioned in the context of financial discrepancies leading to FTX's downfall."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is a subsidiary of FTX, mentioned in the context of financial challenges and the $8 billion liability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is mentioned as a company whose name Bankman-Fried incorrectly stated, indicating a lack of accurate knowledge about its identity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is a hedge fund at the center of the FTX fraud case, and a place where Ellison worked and even slept with Bankman-Fried."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is where Sam Miller worked and was romantically involved with CEO Brody Bankman-Fried, which led to its integration with FTX and unconventional financial practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is a trading firm co-founded by Bankman-Fried, implicated in the fraudulent activities leading to FTX's collapse."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is a trading platform under FTX, involved in financial scandals and excessive risk-taking behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is a crypto trading company involved in the case, which faced financial difficulties in 2022 and was unable to repay customer money to FTX."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research is a sister hedge fund run by Caroline Ellison, implicated in FTX's fraudulent activities and has ties to Sam Bankman-Fried."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda Research, a subsidiary of FTX, is implicated in the testimony for having special privileges and for being used to potentially mislead customers about FTX's operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-11a3202ef6d37f3c721458d4118b84e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7f35c4b6154a8f2343fab7cd419b4f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c51d18a87b8c5bcea42b00475309ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60dd9377ce3b586374dfab3d0a374040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f90dd524447230c0ba9f19ff45aeae94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86186789739ea225fd9dcfdd550e5a3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75d1f9481798c4491cf83bde220a343e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb78a9662e9f89c12554eea5d98b637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6b3e8f9d0eea4170c5afcd8a902604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fd006714e0bf26c23ed69ba354b35b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46cd2916b14e2a6e0e550ee312536887&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d890dfc9208b54ae051d1a3f6f8086&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cef8862c6918d02dd1f5018cabaed6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fcf42217627fbc93f1fe3da4f67854b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAROLINE ELLISON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Caroline Ellison is a key figure in FTX's fraudulent activities, pleaded guilty to charges, and cooperates with the prosecution as a witness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caroline Ellison is implied to have a managerial role at Alameda Research, associated with the company's controversial actions during its financial crisis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caroline Ellison is mentioned alongside Changpeng “CZ” Zhao, suggesting a potential role in FTX's operational decisions that may have affected customer accounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caroline Ellison is the former CEO of Alameda Research, who pleaded guilty to federal criminal charges related to the FTX collapse."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caroline Ellison was the former CEO of Alameda Research, involved in controversial financial decisions and interactions with Chinese officials.&lt;SEP&gt;"Caroline Ellison"&lt;SEP&gt;"Caroline Ellison, after pleading guilty, is a figure who represents the consequences and legal outcomes for individuals involved in the FTX collapse."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caroline Ellison was another hired employee at Alameda Research, one of Bankman-Fried's co-conspirators mentioned in the context of the company's operation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caroline Ellison was the head of Alameda Research and a witness in the FTX fraud trial, with personal and professional entanglements with Bankman-Fried."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caroline Ellison, Bankman-Fried's ex-girlfriend, testified about creating fraudulent balance sheets and misinvesting customer funds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caroline Ellison is a witness in the trial, whose testimony has tied FTX's CEO to the fraudulent activities involving customer funds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caroline Ellison is mentioned as a participant in meetings concerning FTX's financial dealings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7f35c4b6154a8f2343fab7cd419b4f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60dd9377ce3b586374dfab3d0a374040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae72da3d9b8976ac437556b02fe22ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb78a9662e9f89c12554eea5d98b637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d2bd01beb43dfa1ac162f2b78053a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fd006714e0bf26c23ed69ba354b35b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d890dfc9208b54ae051d1a3f6f8086&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f44d1fb769811b62dec26a14ca8e3ba8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cef8862c6918d02dd1f5018cabaed6f0</data>
</node>
