<node id="&quot;MARK COHEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mark Cohen interacts with the jurors, potentially influencing their perception and the trial's atmosphere."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mark Cohen is Sam Bankman-Fried's legal counsel, also involved in the direct examination process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mark Cohen is a defense attorney representing Sam and his colleagues, portraying them as overwhelmed rather than malicious in the context of FTX's collapse."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mark Cohen is a defense attorney with a background as a former federal prosecutor, representing Bankman-Fried in the trial."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mark Cohen is a lawyer representing Sam Bankman-Fried, defending him against fraud allegations, portraying him as acting in good faith and a successful entrepreneur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mark Cohen is the defense attorney representing Sam Bankman-Fried, known for his attempt to use the startup analogy to explain FTX's challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mark Cohen is a defense attorney, noted for his disorganized cross-examination and interaction with jurors and other legal personnel during the trial."</data>
