  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL MEDIA PLATFORM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"TikTok is a social media app heavily used by half of the study participants, particularly popular among kids aged 11 and 12, and associated with significant amounts of screen time.&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is a social media platform where Francesca uploads her content and engages with her followers, including her famous father, highlighting the role of digital media in contemporary language evolution."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is a social media platform where a video highlighting the translation mistranslation issue went viral."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is described as a platform experimenting with a new ad-free subscription tier, indicating its active role in user engagement strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok, a popular social media platform for short-form video content, is a subject to layoffs in various industries, including tech, reflecting broader economic trends."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok, a platform similar to Snapchat, is mentioned in the context of content creation and sharing, with a user sharing personal experiences regarding communication blackouts in Gaza.&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is a technology platform that played a role in a notable event involving Gen Z activism."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is discussed in the context of privacy concerns and data sharing with the Chinese government."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is the social media platform under scrutiny for allegedly tracking users without consent."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is the platform where the conversation between Francesca and Martin Scorsese takes place, highlighting its role in modern communication."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is a social platform that significantly contributed to the viral spread of Si No Estás, resulting in millions of creations and aiding in its massive success."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is criticized by Ohanian for its role as a tool for Chinese government propaganda."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is an app mentioned as being warned by the EU about content risks related to the Israel-Hamas conflict."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is described as a key player in the music industry and launchpad for viral hits and new artists, with initiatives like SoundOn and TikTok Music."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is described as a platform with substantial influence on music consumption and spending, expanding its services to become a partner and competitor in the music world."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok, another app from ByteDance, ranked at No. 5 in the U.S. and has faced government scrutiny and bans due to its China ties."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is a social media platform where young users are not taking candidates seriously, and where Ramaswamy posts receive negative comments."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is the platform where Republican candidates like Mehmet Oz are active, facing challenges in connecting with younger voters."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok is the social media platform that Republican candidates, including Vivek Ramaswamy, are attempting to use to connect with younger demographics, but which is also at the center of national security concerns."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok, a social media platform, is mentioned as a place where safety concerns and videos regarding the Cybertruck are being shared."&lt;SEP&gt;"TikTok, as a social media platform, played a significant role in catapulting the song 'Greedy' to viral success, showcasing the power of social media in modern music promotion.</data>
