  <data key="d1">"Epic Games is a Fortnite publisher involved in legal disputes over app store fees and monopoly claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games is a Fortnite publisher involved in the legal battle against Google over app store fees and monopoly practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games is a company involved in antitrust lawsuits against Google and Apple, seeking to reach Android's user base without Play Store fees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games is involved in a separate antitrust lawsuit against Google, alleging anticompetitive behavior in relation to Google Play and the Android app store."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games is the creator of Fortnite, involved in an antitrust lawsuit against Google regarding app distribution and commission structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games, known for creating Fortnite, is laying off employees in a significant reduction of its workforce."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games, the developer behind Fall Guys, experienced a significant staff reduction as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games is a company that develops games and technologies, including the Epic Games Store."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games is a developer expressing concerns about competition and fair practices, advocating for the removal of payment ties and anticompetitive measures for the benefit of consumers and developers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games is a company pitted against Google and Apple in the trial concerning app store policies and revenue sharing disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games is a publisher that benefited from the Fortnite model, which provided free weekly content updates and capitalized on the gaming engine licensing, leading to significant profits and industry influence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games is recognized as the developer of Fortnite, which is highlighted in the text as a significant gaming platform with a large player base."</data>
