<node id="&quot;STADE DE FRANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stade de France is a venue located in France where the Rugby World Cup match took place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stade de France is the place where the rugby match was played and is noted for its memorable weather and atmosphere."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stade de France is the venue where the semi-final match between England and South Africa will be held."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddd6db649bb44bf1111749979f08db46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb3956171bae9020f5445d66da61b1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa656421859f64e6364cb208c8b769f8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPRINGBOKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Springboks are a South African rugby team that has been influenced by Erasmus's speech, focusing on playing for their country rather than individual glory."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Springboks are the rugby team that won the match, mentioned several times throughout the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddd6db649bb44bf1111749979f08db46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37844ef1f675771afc3c7ac8eac907f6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ALL BLACKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TEAM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The All Blacks are New Zealand's national rugby team, known for their exceptional performance in the Rugby World Cup."&lt;SEP&gt;"The All Blacks are the national rugby team of New Zealand, recognizing the generational change and the importance of the leaders leaving.&lt;SEP&gt;"The All Blacks are the opposing rugby team that lost the match, highlighted in the context of their performance and history."&lt;SEP&gt;"The All Blacks is the New Zealand national rugby team, currently experiencing leadership changes and facing pressure after a historic series loss."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddd6db649bb44bf1111749979f08db46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb3956171bae9020f5445d66da61b1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37844ef1f675771afc3c7ac8eac907f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f31040abd1f07111a95a9467908b1edc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NELSON MANDELA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nelson Mandela is mentioned as an inspiration for 'Live and Let Love', but no further context is given. "&lt;SEP&gt;"Nelson Mandela is referenced symbolically in relation to a historic moment when he handed over the William Webb Ellis Cup to Francois Pienaar, serving as a metaphor for pride and unity.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddd6db649bb44bf1111749979f08db46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ef999d8fd710342d10badbc6cab0ebd</data>
