<node id="&quot;RISK MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Risk Management could involve the team's approach to potential challenges and limitations associated with using certain controllers in the context of first contact with extraterrestrial intelligence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk Management refers to the strategies and processes implemented by sportsbooks to manage the financial risk associated with betting activities and protect their business from loss."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk management involves strategies to identify, assess, and mitigate risks, crucial for the stability of financial institutions and the cryptocurrency market.&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk management is an operational concern in sports betting to minimize potential losses and ensure responsible betting practices.&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk management is a system or set of policies that would have ideally prevented the avoidance of liquidation, relevant to the fraudulent activities at Alameda Research and FTX."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk Management in betting involves strategies to mitigate potential losses, important for responsible gambling and betting success."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk Management is critical for organizations in mitigating various business risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk Management is an essential part of investing, particularly when relying on relative valuation, as it ensures proper evaluation and potential pitfalls are mitigated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk management pertains to the approach of handling the financial and potential losses associated with betting, especially pertinent in sports betting contexts like NBA prop betting."</data>
