<node id="&quot;ALAMEDA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Alameda is a company that was granted special privileges by FTX through coded access. These privileges included unlimited withdrawals and a large line of credit. The misuse of funds led to an $8 billion bug that contributed to FTX's bankruptcy. Wang, as one of the co-founders, had a vested interest in Alameda's management decisions and the company's financial health.&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda is connected to FTX through the borrowing of funds and investment in venture capital, indicating a financial and strategic relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda is one of the organizations where Adam Yedidia worked as a trader and developer, associated with FTX and potentially relevant to the trial."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda is one of the top traders at FTX and is implicated in the misuse of customer deposits according to Yedidia's testimony."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda is mentioned in the context of hiring accountants, relating to FTX's financial management issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alameda is another organization implicated in the case, potentially related to FTX through corporate structure or operation."</data>
