  <data key="d2">chunk-10c4e5dc5e3453b2b2772792a15d6021&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATABASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Database is another technical term that was explained by Bankman-Fried during his testimony, again emphasizing his difficulties with detail-oriented explanations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WIRE FRAUD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wire Fraud is one of the charges against Sam Bankman-Fried, highlighting his alleged illegal financial activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wire fraud involves any scheme to intentionally and willfully deceive another person or entity with a view to obtaining money, property, or causing financial loss, central to the charges against Sam Bankman-Fried."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae72da3d9b8976ac437556b02fe22ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NISHAD SINGH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nishad Singh is a programmer associated with FTX, whose code is mentioned in the context of the changes to the "allow_negative" feature."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nishad Singh is identified as the director of engineering at FTX, who was responsible for reviewing the code that contained the $8 billion bug leading to FTX's downfall."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nishad Singh was another hired employee at Alameda Research, brought in about a month after its founding by Bankman-Fried."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nishad Singh, a longtime family friend of Bankman-Fried, testified about backdating transactions and is a co-conspirator in the fraud."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1fbf2d5f58f4b4f3b25a566059e9283e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86186789739ea225fd9dcfdd550e5a3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cef8862c6918d02dd1f5018cabaed6f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FTX'S RISK ENGINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"FTX's Risk Engine refers to the system designed by FTX to prevent large losses from being spread among customers, which failed in 2020 according to Sam Bankman-Fried's testimony."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULAR CRYPTOCURRENCY VS FUTURES EXCHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regular Cryptocurrency is contrasted with Futures Exchange, with the latter being described as even more akin to a casino due to inherent risks, emphasizing the nature of FTX's business and its eventual downfall."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BUSINESS STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitrage refers to the strategy of profiting from market inefficiencies, which Sam Bankman-Fried implemented at his initial cryptocurrency trading firm, resulting in wildly successful returns before FTX's collapse."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;20% SUCCESS ESTIMATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BUSINESS ESTIMATE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"20% Success Estimate is mentioned by Bankman-Fried regarding the likelihood of success for the cryptocurrency exchange they founded, which is ironic considering the high risk associated with such an estimate in their actual experience.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LACK OF RISK TEAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATIONAL ISSUE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lack of Risk Team is identified by Bankman-Fried as a "big mistake," pinpointing a pivotal oversight in the management structure that contributed to FTX's failure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GARY WANG'S ROLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"POSITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gary Wang was an employee at Alameda Research responsible for programming computers, his role is relevant to understanding the operational aspects of the company he was involved with."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NISHAD SINGH'S HIRING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TEAM DYNAMICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nishad Singh was hired by Bankman-Fried to work at Alameda Research, his inclusion in the team is part of the narrative of building the company's workforce.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAROLINE ELLISON'S ROLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"POSITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Caroline Ellison was another key hire by Bankman-Fried at Alameda Research, her role is part of the larger picture of the company's employment and operational structure.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2a8c789b034881e0489e2514ca89f43e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SINGH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Singh is an employee of Bankman-Fried, involved in financial decisions such as backdating interest payments to inflate FTX's balance sheet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Singh is mentioned as part of the entities involved in activities conducted without apparent regard for financial or strategic oversight."&lt;SEP&gt;"Singh is involved in the case and whose testimony is questioned for potential self-serving motives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Singh is involved in discussions related to FTX's financial crisis and the actions to be taken."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46cd2916b14e2a6e0e550ee312536887&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75d1f9481798c4491cf83bde220a343e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d17241e18008820b7ad93033bc5f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d2bd01beb43dfa1ac162f2b78053a9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WANG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wang is an employee of Alameda Research and testifies about fraudulent practices within FTX, highlighting his role in the company's controversial financial decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wang is another employee mentioned in relation to Alameda Research's financial activities, specifically in the context of maintaining a positive balance sheet for FTX."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wang is similarly implicated in activities allegedly undertaken without proper managerial attention."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wang is another witness whose credibility is under scrutiny, also implicated in the financial controversy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wang is involved in the internal deliberations about FTX's financial status and actions following the discovery of the misuse of customer funds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wang is portrayed as an individual who interacts with the US lawyers and offers cooperation to the government."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75d1f9481798c4491cf83bde220a343e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d2bd01beb43dfa1ac162f2b78053a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6b3e8f9d0eea4170c5afcd8a902604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46cd2916b14e2a6e0e550ee312536887&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d17241e18008820b7ad93033bc5f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f55a016bd0b17ca041315c4764e0812</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MOBILECOIN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"MobileCoin is referenced in relation to a financial decision by FTX, suggested to be used as a backstop liquidity provider."&lt;SEP&gt;"MobileCoin's exploit is an event that caused a significant loss for FTX, around $63 million, affecting its financial stability and prompting decisions on loss absorption."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46cd2916b14e2a6e0e550ee312536887&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d2bd01beb43dfa1ac162f2b78053a9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIAT@FTX&quot;">
