<node id="&quot;CEO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CEO is a chief executive officer, responsible for making high-level managerial decisions, setting company strategy, and overseeing the overall operations and performance of the organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"CEO is a role in which Bankman-Fried should ideally ensure accuracy and strategic oversight, which is called into question by his actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"CEO refers to the Chief Executive Officer, who is not democratically elected in the context of social media companies but has significant control over platform policies and moderation.&lt;SEP&gt;"CEO refers to the professional position responsible for the overall management and strategic direction of the organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"CEO refers to the Chief Executive Officer, a key role in organizational leadership and decision-making."&lt;SEP&gt;"CEO refers to the Chief Executive Officer, typically an individual leading an organization, although not explicitly mentioned in the text, we can infer involvement in the context of product announcement and decision-making processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-28e9b30585d548129498a7b72212205a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1cee016322b4fff7592544dee13c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75d1f9481798c4491cf83bde220a343e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a023f3597d1b07dd8a0fd9389c374620&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-226396bbe23d2faac70b87776260f0ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f6c1af394ff37b622d7c07d89d3dcb3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL FOCUS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
