  <data key="d1">"Free Agency encompasses the period when players can sign new contracts without restraint, often leading to significant shifts in team composition and roster strength.&lt;SEP&gt;"Free Agency is pertinent when evaluating the transferability and trade potential of quarterbacks, adding another layer to performance discussions.&lt;SEP&gt;"Free Agency is a period when players are able to negotiate with teams outside their current contracts, crucial for Shohei Ohtani's considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Free Agency is the period when Major League Baseball players are able to negotiate new contracts with teams, a significant process for player movement and team composition.</data>
