  <data key="d1">"Strategic Surprise is discussed as a recurring issue that impacts military decisions, akin to historical events of surprise attacks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73382d6acae77178bdd8ff0524e2dbcc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JAPAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Japan is identified as a popular destination for Chinese SaaS startups venturing abroad, highlighting its openness to new technologies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan is seen as becoming more attractive for capital deployment, influenced by improved business governance and government initiatives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan is the country where the events of Pulse take place, emphasizing the cultural and geographical setting of the film."&lt;SEP&gt;"The attack on the US naval base at Pearl Harbor in 1941 serves as a historical analogy for unexpected military actions with far-reaching consequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan is the geographical context where significant financial conferences and investment discussions are taking place, highlighting the country's economic recovery and potential."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan is the country where the Pokémon Garden initiative was launched and where the Pokémon franchise has a substantial following, important for understanding the cultural context of the series."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan is mentioned in the context of a rumored coaching opportunity, but it is not directly involved in the current events of the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Japan is the country where Inter Miami will play their match against Vissel Kobe, highlighting the geographical aspect of the event."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-353c6ed9173c906b08964dd951a169f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef44132042667a7d6644713fa3c2b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d73e0c8d557a5b95a2cd1784df8a36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b3955d0292171a9079c933614e401e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73382d6acae77178bdd8ff0524e2dbcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c48d3cbca8e116d392a0e80ba3182b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec68cbf4663aa3c2965292ab6a6ac908&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69ba08263e37f4eeedcb75c834b01904</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AL-QAEDA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Al-Qaeda's attack on the United States on September 11, 2001 is cited as an example of unexpected global security threats."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73382d6acae77178bdd8ff0524e2dbcc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ISIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The spread of ISIS throughout the Middle East in 2014 is used to illustrate the ongoing pattern of strategic surprise and its impact on regional and global security."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73382d6acae77178bdd8ff0524e2dbcc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTELLIGENCE FAILURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intelligence failures are highlighted as a trend with no improvement in early detection of strategic surprises, despite technological advancements in information gathering."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73382d6acae77178bdd8ff0524e2dbcc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;US INTELLIGENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"US intelligence is mentioned in relation to misjudging the threat level of ISIS occupation of Iraq and Syria, indicating a broader issue in intelligence assessment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73382d6acae77178bdd8ff0524e2dbcc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAM RUTHERFORD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sam Rutherford is an Engadget contributor who has provided a screenshot and positive review for Super Mario Bros. Wonder, illustrating the game's enjoyable aspects and design features."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sam Rutherford is an author who writes a review about Super Mario Bros. Wonder for Engadget, providing critical analysis of the game's features and mechanics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPER MARIO BROS. WONDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAME"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Super Mario Bros. Wonder is a platforming RPG that features local multiplayer, allowing four players to choose from classic characters like Mario and Luigi."&lt;SEP&gt;"Super Mario Bros. Wonder is a video game that introduces new mechanics, such as Wonder Flowers, which significantly alter gameplay and add a layer of unpredictability and exploration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Super Mario Bros. Wonder is lauded for its art, animations, and innovative gameplay mechanics like Wonder Seeds that enhance its appeal and longevity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Super Mario Bros. Wonder is an iterative entry in the Mario series, celebrated for its creative and nostalgic elements that differ from the more experimental 3D games."&lt;SEP&gt;"Super Mario Bros. Wonder is described as a game that combines traditional platforming with musical stages and Wonder Seeds, catering to both solo and multiplayer experiences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e567e8d1d0ad018513bd1d3bd3e8f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22c263bbdd03b71b5858208577a9f401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4cd1ccccba403777dc695b70c33ac1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NINTENDO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nintendo is mentioned as the creator of the Super Mario Bros. Movie and the Nintendo Switch game, indicating its organizational role in entertainment and gaming."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nintendo is recognized as a major video game developer addressing concerns about game pacing and level design in Super Mario Bros. Wonder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nintendo is the company behind Super Mario Bros. Wonder, tasked with creating and releasing innovative gaming experiences while maintaining the essence of the classic Mario series."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nintendo is recognized for having a successful year, especially with games that allow players to engage with digital elements in significant ways."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nintendo is the developer company behind The Legend of Zelda series, implicated in decisions about character representation and gender dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nintendo is mentioned in the context of its recent release, Wonder, aligning with the nostalgia trend in the gaming industry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nintendo is the company that develops and releases the Super Mario Bros. Wonder game, known for its success in the gaming industry and major franchises."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df0e11a75346099946cfe8b91ae505b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da113a964d7f484d84be317ff49d0316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4cd1ccccba403777dc695b70c33ac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2434d305c25f623f143e1ae5c98cc67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f5b7fb4d3d9c96668027b20a33fd77</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRINCE FLORIAN OF THE FLOWER KINGDOM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Prince Florian of the Flower Kingdom is the setting where Mario and his crew embark on their mission to restore order, offering a variety of themed levels and hidden features."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BOWSER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bowser is the primary antagonist in the Mario series, whose actions drive the initial conflict in the game by stealing a Wonder Flower and merging with a castle."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WONDER FLOWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wonder Flowers are a central gameplay mechanic in Super Mario Bros. Wonder, changing the rules of the Mario universe and adding new dimensions and challenges to each stage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LUIGI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Luigi is one of the protagonists alongside Mario and Peach, contributing to the diverse group working together in the game."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PEACH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Peach is another central character who participates in the mission to save Prince Florian's land from Bowser's chaos."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YOSHI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Yoshi is included in the group of characters assisting in the game's missions, playing a role in the diverse team dynamic."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOAD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Toad is another regular character from the Mario series who joins the adventure in Super Mario Bros. Wonder."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAISY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Daisy is a new character in Super Mario Bros. Wonder, contributing to the game's cast of heroes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/CHARACTER"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mario is a brand and personality associated with Nintendo, significantly impacting various related products including a movie and a game mentioned in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;"Mario is the primary protagonist and iconic character guiding the team through the game's various missions and levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mario is the central character around whom the entire game series is centered, with his adventures forming the core of the Super Mario Bros. Wonder game experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mario represents a series of characters, including Mario and his friends like Peach, Toad, Nabbit, and Yoshi, who are the humanoid and critter characters in the game."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22c263bbdd03b71b5858208577a9f401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab4cd1ccccba403777dc695b70c33ac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-385774c8f60c29bf8544825b51fafb2c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRE FLOWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"POWER-UP"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fire Flower is a power-up available to Mario in the game, enhancing his abilities and adding a strategic element to gameplay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELEPHANT SUIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"POWER-UP"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Elephant Suit is another power-up option for Mario, providing different gameplay dynamics compared to the Fire Flower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Elephant Suit is mentioned as a gameplay element that could potentially be overpowered, indicating a part of the game's mechanics that players engage with."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUBBLE MUSHROOM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"POWER-UP"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bubble Mushroom is a power-up that offers Mario temporary invincibility and bubble defense, altering his gameplay strategy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DRILL HAT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"POWER-UP"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Drill Hat is a power-up that allows Mario to shoot drills, changing the way he can interact with the game environment and enemies.&lt;SEP&gt;"Drill Hat is another gameplay element mentioned, which is suggested to possibly be overpowered when compared to the Elephant Suit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KO ARENAS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAMEPLAY ELEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"KO Arenas are game levels where players can choose their power-ups and engage with enemy waves, adding a strategic combat element to the gameplay of Super Mario Bros. Wonder."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BREAK TIME LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAMEPLAY LEVEL"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Break Time levels provide short bursts of excitement, offering variety within the game's platforming segments, contributing to the game's overall pacing and player engagement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CUSTOMIZABILITY AND REPLAYABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BADGES SYSTEM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The badges system in Super Mario Bros. Wonder adds customizability and replayability, allowing players to tailor their gameplay experience through the acquisition of beneficial effects during gameplay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECRET NOOKS AND CRANNIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAME FEATURE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Secret nooks and crannies are hidden areas within the levels that players can discover, adding an exploratory and rewarding aspect to the game, enhancing the sense of freedom and engagement within the game world."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNEXPECTED GAME PACING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAMEPLAY EXPERIENCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Unexpected game pacing refers to an infusion of varied level types and dynamics beyond the traditional side-scroller format, which can catch players off guard but enriches the game by providing a diverse and engaging gameplay experience."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SONG INTEGRATED SOUNDTRACKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AUDIO FEATURE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Song integrated soundtracks contribute to the game's atmosphere and immersion, with music that may react to player actions, enhancing the narrative and emotional tone of various game environments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENCOURAGING PHRASES FROM WONDER FLOWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAMEPLAY INTERACTION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wonder Flowers that shout words of encouragement or funny quips as the player runs by serve as interactive in-game dialogue, adding personality and a sense of community to the gameplay experience.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASK THE DEVELOPER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EXTERNAL RESOURCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ask the Developer is a column by Nintendo where insight into game development is shared, which provided inspiration to the creators of Super Mario Bros. Wonder, showcasing Nintendo's engagement with its fan base and developers' creative process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22559ee101cb0fd666f1d8444997ff15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WIGGLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wiggler is mentioned as a rival to be beaten in the game, contributing to the competitive nature of the gameplay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BOO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Boo is used as an example of a notable entity within the game's world, possibly as an obstacle or a playable character."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WONDER SEEDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wonder Seeds are highlighted as a positive addition to the game that subverts player expectations and contributes to the innovation within the 40-year-old franchise."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPER MARIO WORLD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAME"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Super Mario World is referenced as a favorite 2D Mario game, providing a comparison that underscores the innovative qualities of Super Mario Bros. Wonder."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIFFICULTY RATINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAME MECHANIC"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Difficulty Ratings are a feature in Super Mario Bros. Wonder that allow for customized challenge levels, helping to address concerns about pacing and providing a rewarding experience upon completion of 4- and 5-star levels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIDDEN PATHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAME FEATURE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hidden Paths are a gameplay element in Super Mario Bros. Wonder that leads to higher-rated levels, preventing a rush to the end and enriching the gameplay experience."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;5-STAR LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAME LEVELS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"5-star Levels in Super Mario Bros. Wonder are described as balanced and rewarding challenges, contributing to the game's sense of accomplishment without being punishing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RHYTHM STAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAME FEATURE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rhythm Stages are mentioned as a highlighted aspect of the game, providing a fun and engaging element for players to enjoy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADORABLE PENGUINS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The mention of adorable penguins that did not make it into the ice levels indicates a desire for thematic consistency or expansion in the game's world-building."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a6585a0dcb35644d26226a53c2e552c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RANI ZIM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rani Zim is an individual who has made his fortune in food retailing and real estate, and has recently acquired Psagot Investment House."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PSAGOT INVESTMENT HOUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Psagot Investment House is an entity that was bought by Rani Zim, and now holds a significant market cap before its decline."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MIZRAHI TEFAHOT BANK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mizrahi Tefahot Bank is an organization that provided a loan to Rani Zim for the acquisition of Psagot Investment House."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GROUP PSAGOT FOR FINANCE AND INVESTMENTS (TASE: GPST)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Group Psagot for Finance and Investments is the public company that holds Psagot Investment House, with Zim having a stake in it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KIMAT HINAM SUPERMARKET CHAIN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Kimat Hinam supermarket chain is an organization previously managed and sold by Rani Zim, indicating his experience in business operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME PRODUCING REAL ESTATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income producing real estate is described as a domain where Rani Zim had invested, indicating a business activity in property investment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL CENTERS COMPANY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commercial centers company refers to an organization managed by Rani Zim, specialized in commercial property investment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YANIV BENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Yaniv Bender is a person holding a stake in Group Psagot for Finance and Investments, and is mentioned as a potential buyer of Rani Zim's stake."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEREST RATE HIKES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interest Rate Hikes are factors that negatively affect financial markets, particularly impacting entities with leveraged deals like Psagot Investment House."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUDICIAL OVERHAUL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Judicial Overhaul refers to government-promoted changes that negatively influenced financial markets, indirectly affecting Psagot Investment House's performance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONEY LEAVING ISRAEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The outflow of money from Israel due to the judicial overhaul is an event that impacted the financial landscape, including Psagot Investment House's market value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ISRAELI FINANCE INDUSTRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Israeli finance industry is a location where the negative impact of the judicial overhaul and the subsequent war was felt, especially on Psagot Investment House."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAPITAL MARKET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Capital Market is the broader financial ecosystem where Psagot Investment House operates; its vulnerability to external shocks like political events is highlighted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capital Market is the sector where Psagot's challenges in generating profits are highlighted, distinct from real estate or retailing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6065140447da03df7dc2ab7d1a45ab46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a587b83516dbeae088bc5253bf4bfd16</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PSAGOT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Psagot is a business entity discussing challenges in translating growth into profits in the capital market."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a587b83516dbeae088bc5253bf4bfd16</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ZIM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Zim is an individual associated with the acquisition and sale of Psagot, indicating managerial and investment decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a587b83516dbeae088bc5253bf4bfd16</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DANIEL LEVENTHAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Daniel Leventhal is the new chairperson replacing Zim, signaling a change in company leadership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a587b83516dbeae088bc5253bf4bfd16</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICHECK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"AppliCheck is an entity that Psagot sold control of, which is now a separate holding within the business."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a587b83516dbeae088bc5253bf4bfd16</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONEY MARKET FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Money Market Funds are financial products chosen by Psagot's clients, noted for low management fees and profits, contributing to the company's recent losses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a587b83516dbeae088bc5253bf4bfd16</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL INSIGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial insight refers to the understanding required to succeed in the capital market, which is not solely determined by having financial knowledge."</data>
