<node id="&quot;CLIMATE CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Climate Change describes the long-term alteration in global or regional climate patterns, often linked to increased levels of atmospheric CO2 and other greenhouse gases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate Change is a global event that is being affected by and contributes to the dynamics of communication and public engagement, particularly through social media platforms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate Change is an ongoing environmental change leading to hotter summers and more frequent heatwaves, exacerbating the existing disparities in temperature exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate change is highlighted as a major source of distress for Gen Z, influencing their mental health and sustainability concerns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate change is the central theme of the document, concerning sensitivity to surface warming patterns and their implications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate change is the overarching topic of the study, and it affects the research, methodologies, and implications discussed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate change is a central theme of the text, highlighting its devastating impacts and the urgent need for transition to new energy and land use paradigms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate change is the overarching issue affecting scientists and the general public, causing extreme weather events and impacting daily life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate change represents a significant environmental challenge that the Philippines aims to address through sustainable practices and nature-based solutions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate change is considered an event or phenomenon with significant impacts on the deep sea, as discussed by Copley in terms of its impact on oceanic oxygen levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate change is considered an event or phenomenon with significant impacts on the deep sea, as it alters ocean temperature and oxygen levels, thus affecting marine life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate change is highlighted as a threat to the deep sea, affecting its ecosystems and oxygen levels, an aspect of environmental concern in Copley's discussion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate change is impacting the deep ocean by making it warmer, affecting the water's ability to carry dissolved oxygen and speeding up the metabolism of deep sea creatures, leading to a quicker consumption of oxygen."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-17e98775b4d1bd8bda37bdc714c17396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93731230509a7fca03f254c9f181c13a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c328bdbfbbf2a99be338315bcfb7e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63cd65182fe27e88c442d035f5b1524e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8806c4c82c49e6ee7c0ec1d680741efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bdc1dc20f3aad563fcdb030fa03a7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dc0aa3fe6e9c6cdb5632f28ac7664f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4feba597c2dd25bbb78301549e87548c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d88fbb53bb94ff29d726d78158372ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e3a0b2e5f17753a03ce1a08fe3e4d7</data>
