<node id="&quot;APPLE WATCH SE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Apple Watch SE does not have a blood oxygen sensor and is therefore not affected by the import ban on watches with this feature."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apple Watch SE is a product from Apple, recommended as the best smartwatch money can buy, with fitness features and convenient notifications for iPhone users."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apple Watch SE, considered the most affordable smartwatch in the lineup with a comprehensive feature set, now down to $179 after regular sales, suitable for iPhone users with its convenient notifications and integrations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Apple Watch SE is a technology product available at a Black Friday deal, described as an entry-point into the Apple Watch ecosystem for those new to smartwatches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apple Watch SE is unaffected by the import ban, lacking SpO2 sensing capabilities, and represents a portion of Apple's product line that can remain on sale."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apple Watch SE is a new generation smartwatch with features like health and fitness tracking, and it's on sale for budget-conscious consumers during Prime Day."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apple Watch SE is recommended as the most affordable carbon-neutral Apple product, compatible with WatchOS 10 and suitable for health tracking features."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apple Watch SE is an entry-level smartwatch product by Apple, which the latest model is reported to be 20% faster and lighter than, making the comparison relevant to the smartwatch deals discussed.&lt;SEP&gt;"Apple Watch SE is a smartwatch model that offers health and fitness tracking features, with updated software support through WatchOS 10, offering a more affordable alternative to the Apple Watch Series 9."</data>
