  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Killers of the Flower Moon is Scorsese's latest film, demonstrating his continued capability for groundbreaking cinema late in his career."&lt;SEP&gt;"Killers of the Flower Moon is a film based on a nonfiction book that explores the dark history of the Osage murders in the 1920s, adapted by Martin Scorsese."&lt;SEP&gt;"Killers of the Flower Moon is a film by Scorsese that deals with themes of white supremacy and systemic racism, reflecting on societal issues and individual culpability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Killers of the Flower Moon is a historical true crime film directed by Scorsese, inspired by David Grann's book, and follows themes of avarice, violence, and power consolidation in early 20th-century America."</data>
