</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE RATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Rates are indicative of the financial technology affecting borrowing costs and influencing homebuying decisions in the current housing market."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage rates are a component of the financial technology used in the housing market, affecting affordability and sales transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage rates are discussed as a critical economic factor affecting the housing market, having soared due to the Fed's anti-inflation policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage rates are economic indicators that directly influence the affordability and demand in the housing market."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage rates at 8% are discussed as a headwind, affecting housing affordability and market activity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0f67a4fb7eca5299140a7839e542cb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d587ce0c15b675aeafb2497af78d8e0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1ab1bca68b237d4474ab10a17150cde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5db45c54e2afc522f4079d2905b026c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOME PRICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Home prices are a fundamental concept in the housing market affecting affordability and market stability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Home prices' behavior is compared across different historical periods, peaking in 2022 and then remaining stable during the 1980s recession."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0f67a4fb7eca5299140a7839e542cb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1ab1bca68b237d4474ab10a17150cde</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BABY BOOMERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Baby Boomers lived through the civil rights movement and the Vietnam War, indicating their influence on historical and social changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Baby boomers are referenced as a demographic group whose homebuying activity could support the housing market, similar to millennials' current prime homebuying age."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0f67a4fb7eca5299140a7839e542cb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-381b50a9bc37c815d8cd2ef587f31810</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER PRICE INDEX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ECONOMIC INDICATOR"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Consumer price index is a measure of inflation and is one of the key indicators of economic health."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Consumer Price Index is mentioned as having peaked in the 1980s, illustrating the level of inflation that necessitated Federal Reserve intervention."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0f67a4fb7eca5299140a7839e542cb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe7bfbdadb771aa7d84fecfca8ef27e7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VOLCKER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paul Volcker is recognized as the former Chair of the Federal Reserve who implemented policies to combat high inflation in the 1980s, setting a historical precedent for the current economic situation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0f67a4fb7eca5299140a7839e542cb9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAUL VOLCKER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paul Volcker is specifically noted for his aggressive monetary policies during his tenure as Fed Chair, which led to cooling inflation and a subsequent recession in the 1980s."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paul Volcker was a Federal Reserve Chairman in the 1980s, known for combating inflation through interest rate hikes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0f67a4fb7eca5299140a7839e542cb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5db45c54e2afc522f4079d2905b026c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOUSING MARKET BUBBLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'housing market bubble' is used to describe the years of surging home prices that some experts warn could lead to a market crash, similar to concerns in the past."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0f67a4fb7eca5299140a7839e542cb9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBPRIME MORTGAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subprime Mortgages are noted as a factor missing from the current housing market in comparison to the 1980s, indicating a shift in lending practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subprime mortgages are brought up as part of the 2008 housing market crash, contrasted with the current situation where such risky financial products are less prevalent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0f67a4fb7eca5299140a7839e542cb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5db45c54e2afc522f4079d2905b026c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MILLENNIALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GROUP"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Millennials are a demographic group that is currently reaching peak homebuying age, experiencing the housing market conditions described."&lt;SEP&gt;"Millennials are identified as the current demographic reaching the age of prime homebuying, analogous to the baby boomers of the 1980s, contributing to the resilience of the housing market."&lt;SEP&gt;"Millennials are referenced as a comparable previous generation that experienced significant historical events like 9/11 and the U.S. invasion of Iraq, indicating their impact on society."</data>
