  <data key="d2">chunk-e34c4d80597ef64e22796052498f4b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f748ec438c2ae6b09ae2cd8ff3498f8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be55cd201112bf09f4a7ac35e82b7d1c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MASSACHUSETTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Massachusetts is highlighted as a significant location for cranberry farming and the headquarters of Ocean Spray."&lt;SEP&gt;"Massachusetts is identified as the place where cranberry cultivation began in 1816, a key historical location in the development of cranberry agriculture in the U.S."&lt;SEP&gt;"Massachusetts is mentioned as a significant location for cranberry production, cultural significance, and the setting for efforts by individuals like Marcus Urann."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e34c4d80597ef64e22796052498f4b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f748ec438c2ae6b09ae2cd8ff3498f8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be55cd201112bf09f4a7ac35e82b7d1c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRANBERRY CULTIVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cranberry cultivation refers to the process and history of how cranberries have been domesticated and grown, which is a significant event in the transformation of cranberries from wild berries to a prominent agricultural crop."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e34c4d80597ef64e22796052498f4b8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WATER POLLINATION IN CRANBERRIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Water pollination is a unique botanical feature of cranberries, where pollen from flowers is carried by water to fertilize other flowers, as opposed to relying on insects or birds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e34c4d80597ef64e22796052498f4b8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WHOLE GENOME DUPLICATION EVENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Whole genome duplication events are mentioned as significant evolutionary events in the genetic history of cranberries that have led to changes in the genetic makeup of the species."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e34c4d80597ef64e22796052498f4b8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRANBERRY GENOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The cranberry genome is discussed as a subject of scientific study to understand its genetic structure and identify traits for breeding purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e34c4d80597ef64e22796052498f4b8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVOLUTIONARY WAR VETERAN HENRY HALL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Henry Hall is recognized as a historical figure who initiated cranberry cultivation in Massachusetts, contributing significantly to the agricultural development of cranberries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e34c4d80597ef64e22796052498f4b8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WHOLE GENOME DUPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Whole genome duplication is an evolutionary event where two species' genomes combine to create a new, larger genome containing traits of both parental species, often resulting in both gains and losses of genetic diversity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46e47e301c4756471fb5dc36960a527b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GENETIC BOTTLENECKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Genetic bottlenecks occur when a population size is significantly reduced, limiting genetic diversity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46e47e301c4756471fb5dc36960a527b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRANBERRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cranberry refers to the plant species, whose genomic studies provide insights into evolutionary divergence and trait inheritance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46e47e301c4756471fb5dc36960a527b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BLUEBERRY&quot;">
