  <data key="d1">"Ursula Pachl is the deputy director general of BEUC, leading the organization's efforts and providing statements on Meta's actions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EUROPEAN UNION (EU)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"EU is a region where multiple consumer protection organizations are filing complaints against Meta's data tracking and profiling practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"The European Union's GDPR sets a precedent for AI regulation, which California's CPPA is building upon, indicating international relevance and influence on global privacy standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACEBOOK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Facebook is involved in an ongoing antitrust case, facing a possible requirement to sell Instagram and WhatsApp."&lt;SEP&gt;"Facebook is one of Meta's main products and services targeted by the consumer protection organizations' complaints."&lt;SEP&gt;"Facebook, a major social media platform, has been mentioned as a competitor of X, which impacts X's user and engagement metrics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Facebook is referred to as a platform facing challenges in content moderation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Facebook, previously a top-ranking app from Meta, has dropped out of the top 10 in the list of most-downloaded iPhone apps in 2023."&lt;SEP&gt;"Facebook is mentioned as a monolithic social media platform that the fediverse aims to deconstruct into individual components for innovation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Facebook is mentioned as the standard platform whose features and business model users are currently tied to, criticized for its monopolistic control over user data and experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"Facebook is one of Meta's platforms where the ad-free subscription will be offered."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-afd0fcee78f483242cf605dfa283595a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af0301db5f38bf9080adf18f0e753d32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ba125490aad26cd0a87f33374ac9ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb2e2dfb9f20f82cd50e1467190df37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a023f3597d1b07dd8a0fd9389c374620&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0952c6f1db7260a984139b544391d19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91933cfb3e595013e059f4886685740c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DER STANDARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Der Standard is a daily newspaper in Austria where the 'pay-or-consent' model for online advertising was first pioneered."&lt;SEP&gt;"Der Standard is a daily newspaper involved in the context of discussing cookie paywalls and GDPR compliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOYB&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"noyb is a European privacy rights group challenging Meta's tracking and profiling practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"noyb is a consumer rights organization challenging the 'pay or okay' approach to GDPR consent."&lt;SEP&gt;"noyb is a not-for-profit privacy rights organization that has been challenging Meta's consent model since 2021."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af0301db5f38bf9080adf18f0e753d32</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IRELAND’S DATA PROTECTION COMMISSION (DPC)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"DPC is Meta's lead data protection authority in the EU, currently assessing its pay or consent offer for data processing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER ADVOCACY GROUPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Consumer Advocacy Groups are groups that represent the interests of consumers and are actively involved in filing complaints against Meta's practices in the EU."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumer advocacy groups often lobby for stronger privacy protections and could influence or react to the CPPA's regulatory changes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EU MEMBER STATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"EU Member States are the countries within the European Union where the consumer protection organizations involved in the complaint are based."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACEBOOK AND INSTAGRAM USERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Users of Facebook and Instagram are directly impacted by Meta's 'pay-or-consent' model, representing millions of individuals whose data privacy and choices are at stake."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT RULINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court Rulings have previously declared Meta's practices as incompatible with the GDPR, providing a legal precedent for the current complaints."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NETWORK EFFECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Network Effects refer to the phenomenon wherein the value of a service increases with the number of users, which, in Meta's case, makes users less likely to switch due to high subscription fees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COOKIE WALLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cookie Walls are mechanisms used by some publishers to enforce user consent on their websites, similar to Meta's 'pay-or-consent' model, and have been subject to legal challenges."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEWSPAPER READERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Newspaper Readers are implicitly affected by Meta's model due to the impact on publishers' advertising strategies that rely on reader consent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a9132e992f6e5d72e5c33952b267b9b8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUSTRIA’S DPA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Austria’s Data Protection Authority is involved in making a decision regarding the legality of cookie paywalls."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EUROPEAN COURT OF JUSTICE (CJEU)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"European Court of Justice is the potential long-term decision maker in the case of the 'pay or okay' model for cookie consent."&lt;SEP&gt;"The European Court of Justice (CJEU) made a ruling that affects the application of the reciprocity principle in EU member states."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7f5ee7f196a4e1405812f1ee34113944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER PROTECTION COORDINATION (CPC)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CPC is an EU body that coordinates action on consumer protection concerns."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EUROPEAN COMMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"European Commission oversees Meta's compliance with the Digital Markets Act (DMA) and Digital Services Act (DSA), which include restrictions on personal data use for advertising and requirements for user consent."&lt;SEP&gt;"The European Commission is enforcing the Digital Services Act (DSA) and conducting an investigation into Elon Musk’s X (X) for potential breaches of DSA rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"The European Commission is acknowledged for its role in addressing concerns about the ruling and proposing solutions for copyright payment issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7f5ee7f196a4e1405812f1ee34113944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4931d9af8c9e38d233aa70ca5cfb9f45</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GDPR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"GDPR is a regulatory framework that includes requirements for user consent for data processing and has relevance to Meta's cookie consent model."&lt;SEP&gt;"GDPR refers to the General Data Protection Regulation, a fundamental legal framework in the EU that Commissioner mentions complies with."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL MARKETS ACT (DMA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"DMA is a new EU law that subjects large online platforms to specific restrictions, including on the use of personal data for advertising, requiring user consent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL SERVICES ACT (DSA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"DSA is a new EU law mandating clear and easy user consent for data processing, applicable to large online platforms like Meta's social networks."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Digital Services Act (DSA) is the European regulation under which X is being investigated for potential breaches of rules concerning illegal content and other issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"DSA refers to the legislation that places obligations on very large online platforms (VLOPs) to combat the spread of disinformation and ensure algorithmic societal risks are mitigated."&lt;SEP&gt;"DSA is the digital governance regulation related to online advertising that the controversy revolves around."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-00d1f70c791dd98fbfdf4b4040f28fb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-674db37cf38da4f0619869a8020ebf71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4931d9af8c9e38d233aa70ca5cfb9f45</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COOKIE PAYWALLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cookie paywalls are mechanisms used by websites and online services to block user access unless certain conditions are met, often requiring payment or consent to bypass them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA PROTECTION AUTHORITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Data protection authorities are regulatory bodies responsible for enforcing data protection laws and handling complaints related to GDPR and privacy issues, such as cookie paywalls."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Consent is a fundamental requirement under GDPR for lawful processing of personal data, which must be freely given, specific, informed, and unambiguous."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRIVATE DATA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Private data refers to information that is personal identifiable information about individuals, which is subject to protection under data privacy laws like GDPR."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BEHAVIORAL ADVERTISING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Behavioral advertising is a form of targeted advertising that uses personal data to analyze and predict user behavior, which is a concern in privacy regulations like GDPR."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;USER REPORTING AND DISCLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Improving user reporting and disclosure around ads/sponsored content is an action taken by Meta in response to consumer protection complaints."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL COINS AND VIRTUAL GIFTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Digital coins and virtual gifts refer to Meta's initiatives within its platform, which are also subject to transparency and disclosure requirements under consumer protection laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f933411d207962ca09b657088999562</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Consumer Regulation refers to legislative measures that aim to protect consumers, including provisions against unfair design choices like dark patterns in payment interfaces."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffaf6bf4dbb1bde81d794081c07c0080</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT INTERFACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment Interface is the digital platform where consumers interact with payment options, which is subject to regulation concerning fair design choices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffaf6bf4dbb1bde81d794081c07c0080</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER PROTECTION AND PRIVACY LAWS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Consumer Protection and Privacy Laws are legal frameworks aimed at protecting consumer rights and privacy, which include regulations against unfair online practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffaf6bf4dbb1bde81d794081c07c0080</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DARK PATTERNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dark Patterns are deceptive design choices in technology interfaces meant to influence user behavior unethically, particularly targeted by regulations in the consumer protection laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffaf6bf4dbb1bde81d794081c07c0080</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNFAIR CHOICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Unfair Choices refers to online practices that mislead or disadvantage consumers by presenting choices in a deceptive manner.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffaf6bf4dbb1bde81d794081c07c0080</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATORY FRAMEWORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulatory Frameworks consist of legal provisions and regulations designed to prevent unfair practices, including those related to online consumer choices and privacy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffaf6bf4dbb1bde81d794081c07c0080</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARIA RUGENSTEIN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maria Rugenstein is an academic affiliated with Colorado State University, involved in climate change research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maria Rugenstein is an academic affiliated with Colorado State University, involved in climate-related research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maria Rugenstein is an author associated with the study on climate sensitivity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8806c4c82c49e6ee7c0ec1d680741efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bdc1dc20f3aad563fcdb030fa03a7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARK ZELINKA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mark Zelinka is a researcher at Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory, also engaged in climate-related studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mark Zelinka is a researcher at Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory, contributing to climate studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mark Zelinka is an author associated with the study on climate sensitivity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8806c4c82c49e6ee7c0ec1d680741efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bdc1dc20f3aad563fcdb030fa03a7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KRISTOPHER B. KARNAUSKAS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Kristopher B. Karnauskas is a researcher with the University of Colorado Boulder, contributing to climate science research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kristopher B. Karnauskas is an author associated with the study on climate sensitivity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8806c4c82c49e6ee7c0ec1d680741efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAULO CEPPI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paulo Ceppi is an author associated with the study on climate sensitivity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIMOTHY ANDREWS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Timothy Andrews is an author associated with the study on climate sensitivity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLIMATE SENSITIVITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Climate Sensitivity is discussed as a measure affected by the pattern effect and relevant to future climate projections and historical patterns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate sensitivity quantifies the Earth's surface warming response to a doubling of carbon dioxide relative to preindustrial levels, directly affecting climate predictions and response strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Climate sensitivity refers to how sensitive the climate system is to alterations in concentration of greenhouse gases and other radiative forcings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9bdc1dc20f3aad563fcdb030fa03a7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281967d9b07cd6cdb5934df0e6537309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GREENHOUSE GASES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Greenhouse Gases are gases that contribute to the greenhouse effect and are mentioned as a factor affecting climate dynamics and surface temperature patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;"Greenhouse gases are contributing to the global energy surplus in Earth's atmosphere, playing a key role in the global warming process described in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greenhouse gases are responsible for trapping heat in the atmosphere, contributing to global warming and climate change that affects deep sea oxygen levels and ecosystems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76dc3420a9c483c16a25c9a5a3d26c60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RADIATIVE FORCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Radiative forcing is the change in energy fluxes caused by alterations in factors like greenhouse gas concentrations, impacting Earth's climate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiative forcing refers to the imbalance in incoming and outgoing energy in the Earth's climate system, which models and observations aim to quantify and understand in the context of climate change."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9bdc1dc20f3aad563fcdb030fa03a7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WATER VAPOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Water vapor is a greenhouse gas that increases in concentration with warming and affects the climate feedback mechanisms as described in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water vapor is the medium from which SmartFarm and the hydrogel technology capture moisture for water extraction purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water vapor is the raw material captured by the hydrogel-based device to produce water."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b35fcf151f20a401d073e4c43ff0aeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0897d199d83904904c800e61d22f120b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRATOCUMULUS CLOUDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stratocumulus clouds, located primarily over the oceans, are a type of low-lying cloud that can reflect solar radiation and thereby have a cooling effect on the planet's temperature, mentioned as part of the feedback loop in the study.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TROPOSPHERIC INVERSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tropospheric inversion refers to atmospheric layers where the temperature increases with altitude, which can influence cloud formation and the climate sensitivity feedback loop as described in the study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WESTERN PACIFIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The western Pacific is identified as a climate sweet spot where significant warming leads to widespread effects that stabilize the atmosphere and promote cloud formation that cools the planet, as discussed in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;"Western Pacific is highlighted as a region where significant climate feedbacks and warming patterns have been observed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76dc3420a9c483c16a25c9a5a3d26c60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EASTERN PACIFIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The eastern Pacific is noted for cooling despite overall global warmth, highlighting regional differences in surface warming patterns discussed in the study.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCEAN AND ATMOSPHERIC OSCILLATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Oscillations involving the ocean and atmosphere are mentioned as natural processes that impact the evolution of surface temperature and climate feedbacks in the study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINENTAL BOUNDARY CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Continental boundary conditions are natural factors that influence climate and surface temperature patterns, part of the variety of processes affecting climate sensitivity as mentioned in the study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ICE SHEETS AND SEA ICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ice sheets and sea ice are also significant factors affecting global temperature and climate feedbacks, emphasized in the study's discussion on regional surface warming patterns."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLIMATE MODELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Climate models are tools used in the study to simulate and understand climate sensitivity and the effects of radiative forcing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RADIATIVE IMBALANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Radiative Imbalance describes the difference between incoming and outgoing radiation at Earth's atmosphere, which is crucial for understanding climate change and the pattern effect."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiative imbalance refers to the disparity between incoming solar radiation absorbed by Earth and outgoing terrestrial radiation; it's a fundamental concept in understanding the climate system's energy balance and is central to the study's analysis of climate sensitivity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76dc3420a9c483c16a25c9a5a3d26c60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSIENT CLIMATE CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transient climate change is a state used in models to simulate temporary changes in the climate system, relevant to understanding how climate sensitivity might manifest in short-term versus long-term scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GLOBAL TEMPERATURE CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Global Temperature Change is a measure of the overall change in Earth's temperature and is central to the discussion of climate sensitivity and feedbacks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Global temperature change is a measure of the overall warming or cooling trend of the planet's surface, closely linked to the study's focus on climate sensitivity and feedback mechanisms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76dc3420a9c483c16a25c9a5a3d26c60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b6f164bfb3e14104317937c9ce0957</data>
