  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ROSTER PERCENTAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Roster Percentage refers to the proportion of a player's team that is made up of them, a statistic often used in fantasy football leagues to gauge player importance and availability.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAREER HIGHS AND LOWS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Career Highs and Lows is a term used to discuss the peak and troughs in a player's professional performance history, crucial for evaluating player potential and past achievements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FANTASY POINTS PER GAME (FPTS/G)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fantasy Points Per Game is a common metric used in fantasy football to measure a player's contribution to a team's score, combining the points scored in receptions, rushing, and receiving yards, and sometimes touchdowns."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WIDE RECEIVERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wide Receivers are a key position group in American football, specialized in catching passes and contributing to a team's passing game, discussed extensively in fantasy football analyses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wide receivers are mentioned as a focal point in the fantasy football rankings and discussions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3aa95065bfc8cb3deb1c5623341a72e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;QUARTERBACKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Quarterbacks are a critical position in American football, primarily responsible for directing the team's offense and throwing passes, their performance is a significant aspect of fantasy football scoring."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFENSIVE PLAYERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Defensive Players refer to the positions on the defensive side of the football team, such as linemen and secondary players like cornerbacks and safeties, their stats are also tracked in fantasy football leagues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FANTASY FOOTBALL DRAFTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fantasy Football Drafts are the initial selections made by fantasy football players in creating their teams for each season, a foundational event in the league's sport.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FREE AGENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Free Agents are players who are not currently on a team and are open to negotiations or signings, a common occurrence in the free agency period of the NFL season affecting team compositions and potential player performances.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE RUMORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Trade Rumors are speculative discussions about potential player trades between teams, impacting team dynamics and strategies prior to or during the trade deadline in the NFL season."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GAME SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Game Schedule is the timetable of upcoming games in the NFL season, vital for fantasy football players when setting their lineups and strategies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PPR (POINTS PER RECEPTION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PPR (Points Per Reception) is a scoring format in fantasy football that awards points for each reception, incentivizing targeted pass-catching players.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SNAP SHARES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Snap Shares indicate the amount of time a player is on the field during a game, reflecting their involvement and potential impact on actual player performance.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLEX POSITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Flex Position is a category in some fantasy football leagues that allows a player to be used in more than one position, often wide receiver or running back, adding versatility to a team's roster.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BYE WEEKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bye Weeks are periods when teams do not play an actual game during the NFL season, affecting player health and team dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bye weeks are a scheduling aspect of fantasy football that impacts competitiveness and player availability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bye weeks refers to the scheduled breaks in the fantasy football leagues where teams do not play."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3aa95065bfc8cb3deb1c5623341a72e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
