<node id="&quot;DRAFT KEEPER LEAGUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Draft Keeper Leagues are a subtype of fantasy football leagues where teams must keep drafted players for a full season, adding an element of roster management over time.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KICKOFFS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Kickoffs are the beginning of a football game, where one team kicks the ball to the other, often leading to statistical opportunities for the kicking team to score and the receiving team to defend, important in fantasy football kickoff and punt return scoring.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIELD GOALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Field Goals are a method of scoring in football where one team kicks the ball through the opponent's goalposts, worth three points and considered when evaluating a team's field goal kickers in fantasy football scoring."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFENSIVE TOUCHDOWNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Defensive Touchdowns are touchdowns scored by defensive players, such as interception and fumble recoveries, worth extra points in fantasy football scoring systems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PASS INTERCEPTION RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pass Interception Returns are when a defensive player recovers a fumble or an intercepted pass and returns it for touchdown, a notable event in fantasy football that can boost a defensive player's contribution to a team's score.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6406f9d6e705b4533df5fb61e6a3b60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DROPBACK ATTEMPTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
