<node id="&quot;MENTAL HEALTH ASSESSMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mental Health Assessment is a process of evaluating an individual's mental health status, essential in determining the risk of depression or suicide among teenage patients and their suitability for programs like Caring Contacts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5467fd8b3b82a317c34edd9694ba2da9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEPRESSION AMONG TEENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Depression Among Teens highlights the significance of teenage depression as a contributing factor to suicide risk, an issue Children's Nebraska addresses through its Caring Contacts program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5467fd8b3b82a317c34edd9694ba2da9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL WORKER-PATIENT RELATIONSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Social Worker-Patient Relationship is pivotal in healthcare settings, where a positive and trusting connection is fostered between social workers and teenage patients to encourage ongoing treatment and follow-up care."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5467fd8b3b82a317c34edd9694ba2da9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY MENTAL HEALTH RESOURCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Mental Health Resources encapsulate the support systems on a community level that may complement programs like Caring Contacts, providing a broader safety net for teen mental health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5467fd8b3b82a317c34edd9694ba2da9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERVISORY TEAM AT HOSPITAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
