<node id="&quot;STEPHEN KING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rural Maine is depicted as the setting for King's 'Salem’s Lot, grounding the supernatural elements of the story in a real-world, relatable location."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stephen King contributes to the anthology as a cameo character."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stephen King is acknowledged for his cameo as a hillbilly character in the Creepshow anthology."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stephen King is recognized for his contributions to the horror genre, specifically compared to his portrayal of a hillbilly in a one-person show."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stephen King makes a cameo performance in the Creepshow anthology, which is part of the Halloween countdown event."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stephen King is a renowned author who modernized vampire fiction with his novel ’Salem’s Lot, which blends the horror of rural Maine society with the concept of vampirism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stephen King is an author whose works have inspired numerous film adaptations, particularly in the horror genre, such as The Mist and The Expanse."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stephen King is renowned for his contributions to horror and suspense literature, with numerous adaptations exploring the genre's dark themes. Beyond film, his work includes novels, short stories, and non-fiction pieces, influencing a wide array of media and discussions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fef44132042667a7d6644713fa3c2b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-802f084551d9a01a17a1d6b398dfbcb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d028f70e89e19f331a24fd76e17b9358&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff21cbef1fa73bc422c512dda89c07b</data>
