  <data key="d1">"Startups are companies that are at the forefront of developing and applying AI, including those working on Large Language Models (LLM&lt;SEP&gt;"Startups are recognized as key players that can fill gaps in AI service offerings, drive third-party adoption through open source, and innovate in specific industry applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Startups focus on specific niches where they can innovate and provide solutions that larger companies may not be equipped to handle, creating opportunities for differentiation and market penetration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Startups refer to companies like Neeva, Twiggle, and Deft, which are in the process of developing and competing in the e-commerce search market and face unique challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;"Startups are small, innovative companies aiming to bring new products to market, often depending on larger corporations for support and resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country has a significant startup ecosystem with 9,000 startups, indicating a vibrant and active business environment."</data>
