</node>
<node id="&quot;CALIFORNIA’S PRIVACY PROTECTION AGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"California’s Privacy Protection Agency is the state privacy regulator tasked with setting rules for digital giants, particularly those in AI, acting as a guardian of data privacy for California residents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTOMATED DECISIONMAKING TECHNOLOGY (ADMT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ADMT stands for Automated Decisionmaking Technology, also known as AI and is the focus of privacy rules being drafted by the CPPA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CALIFORNIA RESIDENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"California residents are the individuals whose data privacy is being protected and to whom the opt-out and access rights will apply under the new AI regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CALIFORNIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY ENVIRONMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"California is identified as having a complex regulatory environment that significantly impacts Cruise's operations and strategic decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"California is the location where the CPPA regulates AI and where the draft regulations are being formulated, affecting the local and potentially global AI landscape."&lt;SEP&gt;"California is the state where the proposed regulatory framework for Automated Decision-Making and Technology (ADMT) is being considered, indicating its relevance to the legal context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a86d099cd55788febb68bb6f9dd8c6a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c6d7259cf4321bf0a7659f23e160b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CALIFORNIA CONSUMER PRIVACY ACT (CCPA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CCPA is a law that came into effect in California in 2020, which the CPPA uses as a foundation for its AI regulations, focusing on consumers' rights to access and control their data."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPT-OUT RIGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The opt-out right allows California residents to deny their data being used for automated decisionmaking, with certain exemptions, as part of the CPPA's approach to AI regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECURITY PURPOSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Security purposes are one of the exemptions under the proposed AI regulations where data can be used without opt-out, related to preventing, detecting, and investigating security incidents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FRAUD PREVENTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fraud prevention is another concept within the exemptions of the AI regulations, allowing the use of data for preventing fraud."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Safety, aiming to protect consumers' life and physical safety, is another exemption under the AI regulations where data can be used without opt-out."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOOD OR SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"When a consumer requests a good or service, their data might be used without the need for opt-out under the proposed AI regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CALIFORNIA'S BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
