</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA CONTROLLERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Data controllers are responsible for processing personal data under GDPR and similar regulations, a role that would also be involved in compliance with the CPPA's AI guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA PROCESSORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Data processors handle data on behalf of the data controller, a role that would be impacted by new AI-specific regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MACHINE LEARNING MODELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Machine learning models are part of AI technology; their development, use, and regulation could be affected by the draft rules focusing on automated decisionmaking."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAWMAKERS AND LEGISLATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lawmakers and legislators are integral to the creation and refinement of laws like the CCPA and GDPR, and would be involved in discussions around AI regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA SUBJECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Data subjects are individuals whose data is processed and whose rights need protection; they are central to the discussion on AI regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENCRYPTION STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Encryption standards are essential for securing data, which would be pertinent in the context of AI regulations regarding data protection and privacy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANTICIPATED OPPOSITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Anticipated opposition likely refers to entities or groups that may challenge or argue against the proposed AI regulations, reflecting the democratic process in regulatory development."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL PLATFORMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Digital platforms are the primary channels through which music is now discovered and enjoyed, playing a crucial role in independent artists' ability to reach audiences worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"Digital platforms, such as social media and e-commerce, could be significantly affected by AI regulations due to their reliance on data analytics and automation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Digital platforms like YouTube and SoundCloud are mentioned as alternatives for music distribution, which has impacted the traditional role of music labels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b6ec12ff3d2abe7cec2701182e5fd433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beaa67873e1ff1fc80cbec5329c8d8d4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CROSS-BORDER DATA TRANSFERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cross-border data transfers become relevant in AI regulation, given the global nature of technology companies and data flows."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL RIGHTS MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Digital rights management is a system for protecting copyrights and managing access to digital media, which could be relevant in the context of controlled AI technology access."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feec4bb36bedcf009ab1afa8484aa0db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTOMATED DECISION-MAKING AND TECHNOLOGY (ADMT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ADMT refers to technologies that process personal data for decision-making purposes, which becomes legal in the California context with certain thresholds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1c6d7259cf4321bf0a7659f23e160b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLICLY ACCESSIBLE PLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Publicly Accessible Place is a context in which profiling consumers' data is considered for ADMT, suggesting regulatory interest in privacy during interactions with businesses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1c6d7259cf4321bf0a7659f23e160b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROFILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Profile involves using ADMT to make decisions about consumers based on their status as employees, contractors, applicants, or students, or where they are located."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1c6d7259cf4321bf0a7659f23e160b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECURITY, FRAUD PREVENTION, SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPTS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are exemptions cited by businesses for legal ADMT use, indicating the conditions under which automated decision-making is permitted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1c6d7259cf4321bf0a7659f23e160b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRE-USE NOTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pre-use Notices are requirements for businesses to inform consumers about the use of ADMT, ensuring transparency and the exercise of consumer rights.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1c6d7259cf4321bf0a7659f23e160b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CCPA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CCPA refers to the California Consumer Privacy Act, which outlines regulations and rights concerning consumer data, including those related to ADMT."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1c6d7259cf4321bf0a7659f23e160b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC COMPONENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public Component is part of the CPPA's consultation process, indicating an avenue for public participation and input on the proposed regulations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1c6d7259cf4321bf0a7659f23e160b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;META, OPENAI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Meta and OpenAI are local giants that might push back against the proposed ADMT regulations, reflecting the potential impact on major AI entities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1c6d7259cf4321bf0a7659f23e160b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CCPA CONSULTATION&quot;">
