<node id="&quot;FORTNITE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GAME"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fortnite is a battle royale game that experienced significant growth and influence on the gaming industry and esports, becoming a model for live service updates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fortnite is a highly successful game developed by Epic Games, featuring a large player base and concurrent users."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fortnite is a title developed by Epic Games, at the center of the antitrust case against Google."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fortnite is an Epic Games product at the center of their strategy to challenge Google's app store dominance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fortnite is a popular free-to-play game that generates revenue through in-game purchases and is at the center of Epic's legal actions against Google and Apple."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fortnite is identified as a shared virtual experience app, relevant to the discussion on interoperability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fortnite is described as a battle royale-style game that has captivated a huge player base, including a major nostalgia trend in entertainment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b5f3c79911cd9857a69ceaa748a8028&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82ef6612b6aebc4c34f55e1e050f5dad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0dc7f087fbb6c7d7f29c2bf4214f618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2434d305c25f623f143e1ae5c98cc67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f23c92284d2cb6a47cffaad94ad0623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74afcc7f25a7f17fb6e289a785fd6dd7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PHIL SCHILLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Phil Schiller is mentioned by Tim Sweeney as having attended the trial with him, implying his role related to Epic Games' legal struggle."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Courts represent the legal venue where the antitrust trial is being conducted and where the jury is deciding the case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHERMAN ANTITRUST ACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Sherman Antitrust Act is a landmark federal statute passed in 1890, which is a critical legal foundation for the antitrust lawsuit brought by Epic Games against Google."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;US V. MICROSOFT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"US v. Microsoft is referenced as a historical precedent where major antitrust action led to change in the tech industry, used by Tim Sweeney to illustrate the importance of the current case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EPIC GAMES LAWSUITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The series of lawsuits filed by Epic Games against Google forms the core subject of the article, highlighting the ongoing battle for market freedom."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JURY VERDICT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The rapid verdict by the jury is a pivotal moment in the antitrust trial, demonstrating the effectiveness of the legal system in addressing complex tech antitrust issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANTITRUST PRACTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Antitrust practices encompass the strategies and actions taken by companies like Google and Apple that may restrict competition and affect fairness in the market, a central theme in the dispute."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antitrust practices refer to the methods used by companies, including Google, to maintain or establish a dominant market position, potentially leading to reduced competition and consumer harm."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f812fe7c8b6ca1ce43ad8986b05a7fef</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEVELOPER NEGOTIATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Negotiations with developers, carriers, and OEMs are tactics employed by Google, as revealed in the trial, to maintain its market hold and to deter competition."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEVELOPER PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Developer payments are part of Google's alleged practices to influence the market and prevent competitors from gaining traction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GAME DEVELOPER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Game developers, such as Epic Games, are key players in the antitrust case, as they challenge the practices that affect their market presence and operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CROSS-PROMOTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cross-promotion refers to the strategy of bundling products, like Fortnite with other services or products, which is a subject of the legal challenge posed by Epic Games against Google's practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMARTPHONE MANUFACTURERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Smartphone manufacturers, like OnePlus, are part of the ecosystem affected by Google's alleged secret deals and monopolistic tactics targeted by Epic Games in their lawsuit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CARRIERS AND OEMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Carriers and OEMs are implicated in the legal battle due to Google's secret dealings with them, impacting the market diversity for services like Fortnite."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JURY MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Jury members are the individuals who deliberate and decide within the courtroom, forming the backbone of the judicial process in the antitrust case against Google."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURTROOM SETTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The courtroom is the setting where the antitrust trial unfolds and where the jury listens to evidence and testimonies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3b3bb643528323d58684e2d810b05225</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EPIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Epic is depicted as an organization that develops processes and leadership structures for maintaining integrity and fairness within its operations, but faces allegations of destroying conversations related to antitrust issues and wrongdoing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic is portrayed as a company involved in a legal dispute with Apple over app store practices, aiming for a change in Google's payment system policy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bdfdd7bc3cc52c359502c3c03b84e92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f812fe7c8b6ca1ce43ad8986b05a7fef</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACTIVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMPANY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Activision is a company that was purportedly building its own mobile app store, which was disbanded after signing a deal with Google. The deal reportedly dissuaded Activision from launching their own store, and it is suggested that they may have intended to prevent competition against Google's platform."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f812fe7c8b6ca1ce43ad8986b05a7fef</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RIOT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMPANY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Riot is a company that planned to distribute League of Legends through its own website, disrupted by Google's intervention with a payoff to continue sales through Google Play.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f812fe7c8b6ca1ce43ad8986b05a7fef</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ALLEGED DEVELOPER COMPANIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Alleged developer companies are mentioned as entities that faced the destruction of conversation threads related to antitrust issues and are part of the dispute with Google over its practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f812fe7c8b6ca1ce43ad8986b05a7fef</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOOGLE SENIOR EXECUTIVES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"POSITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Google senior executives are key players who were able to access the internal documents before the trial began, as mentioned in the context of the email sent by Epic in 2019."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f812fe7c8b6ca1ce43ad8986b05a7fef</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTARY EVIDENCE&quot;">
