</node>
<node id="&quot;UNREAL ENGINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Unreal Engine is a game engine developed by Epic Games, which has seen adoption in various industries beyond games."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unreal Engine is a tool under the umbrella of Epic Games, showcasing Epic's interest in supporting developers across various software creation tools, not just gaming.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f23c92284d2cb6a47cffaad94ad0623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e1f84d5dd7a4705356c1c6f54f888e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EPIC GAMES STORE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Epic Games Store is an online digital distribution service that offers games and provides solutions for compatibility issues with the PS5 DualSense."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games Store is depicted with a potential business model of aggressively paying for exclusive games to attract users, differentiating its model from that of Linux."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games Store is operated by Epic Games, featuring both gaming titles and various other software and productivity tools, indicating its position as a broader platform than just a game store.&lt;SEP&gt;"Epic Games Store's strategy is focused on aggressively acquiring users, primarily through exclusive game offerings, to support their platform."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-97e661d01459ff3bc6d4add99ce21553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e1f84d5dd7a4705356c1c6f54f888e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3550a05ec2b3b6d1c8f2f0f7e7da1465</data>
