</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLE INC.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Apple Inc. is involved in the litigation with Epic Games over app store restrictions, a counterpart in the case with Epic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apple Inc. is the parent company of Apple, involved in navigating the import ban and patent infringement issues related to its products, especially the Apple Watch."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apple Inc. is the tech company involved in the import bans and product features under discussion, central to the context of the narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apple Inc. is the company behind MacBook Pro models, pivotal in setting industry standards and influencing technology trends."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b76c81c445c4cc4d927995e223dd924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f23c92284d2cb6a47cffaad94ad0623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74cf41504f309de964b31f8d5560059b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59ecd88b784f45eb95c2455a5e4c281b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LINUX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Linux is implied to have issues with compatibility, possibly in user-friendliness or the ecosystem, which is a point of discussion in the gaming community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Linux is referred to as a problem, likely in the context of software development and gaming, suggesting its significance in the tech industry."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-97e661d01459ff3bc6d4add99ce21553</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STEAM DECK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Steam Deck is a gaming device not specifically mentioned as discounted during Black Friday, but related in the context as an alternative device for which Samsung microSD cards are recommended."&lt;SEP&gt;"Steam Deck is praised for its hardware, indicating it as a notable piece of technology."&lt;SEP&gt;"Steam Deck is referenced as a device used by gamers, particularly for cross-platform gaming experiences, showcasing advancement in gaming technology.&lt;SEP&gt;"Steam Deck is a handheld gaming console, with its original version often criticized for poor battery life, which has been significantly improved in the Steam Deck OLED model."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Steam Deck is the branded product from Valve, indicating its identity within the marketplace."&lt;SEP&gt;"Steam Deck is the handheld gaming device being updated and set for release, with a hybrid console functionality as a side goal."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Steam Deck is the primary subject of the article, focusing on its OLED upgrade, performance improvements, and associated pricing changes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6caab48b5a0a481883dca5f050484463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd3585b134d2a3d4e91ee558c31ff3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da113a964d7f484d84be317ff49d0316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b193f671609eff98c5bca79a8edddd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28d3ab2cd59881d476cd7d5c2c221f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97e661d01459ff3bc6d4add99ce21553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-112e1439a6a907f08bfa2f8064a6934e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VALVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Valve is a company mentioned as developing future handheld gaming hardware and working on improving SteamOS for both handhelds and larger displays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Valve is a company responsible for developing and selling the Steam Deck OLED, indicating its role as the manufacturer and provider of the device."&lt;SEP&gt;"Valve is a developer and seller of gaming hardware, specifically the Steam Deck and its OLED iteration, highlighting their role in the gaming industry and their relationship with consumers and developers through product enhancements and updates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Valve is described as the developer of the Steam Deck gaming console and its upgrades, including the Steam Deck OLED, demonstrating their role in the gaming industry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Valve is mentioned as the origin of the arbitrary decision that may have influenced the creation of the 70/30 revenue split, which is significant to the context of the legal dispute regarding app store revenue distribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Valve is recognized for its hardware development, specifically the Steam Deck, and is discussed in relation to user support and user base growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Valve is the company that has released the Steam Deck OLED as a mid-cycle refresh, similar to updates made by other companies in the tech industry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Valve is a company that designs, develops, and distributes gaming hardware and digital gaming platforms, with announcements on new devices such as the Steam Deck OLED."&lt;SEP&gt;"Valve is a company that has announced the Steam Deck OLED, a handheld gaming device, as well as making changes to its existing product lineup and pricing strategy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6caab48b5a0a481883dca5f050484463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd3585b134d2a3d4e91ee558c31ff3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97e661d01459ff3bc6d4add99ce21553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28d3ab2cd59881d476cd7d5c2c221f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7d18ee3e795fba2189434b856857270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-112e1439a6a907f08bfa2f8064a6934e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0b819c0da65f86531de93e4b4c5c865</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGGRESSIVE PURSUIT MODEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Aggressive pursuit model is a strategy mentioned previously, contrasting the approach of Epic Games Store towards user acquisition and game exclusivity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aggressive pursuit model is mentioned as a strategy of Epic Games Store, contrasting with the approach towards Linux as described earlier."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-97e661d01459ff3bc6d4add99ce21553</data>
</node>
