  <data key="d2">chunk-4b35bc6113a75b2108aa75e718271e05</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VPN USES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"VPN uses" refers to the traditional and non-traditional purposes for utilizing Virtual Private Networks, such as protecting internet traffic and accessing geographically restricted content.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b35bc6113a75b2108aa75e718271e05</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEVICE COMPATIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Device Compatibility refers to the range of different hardware devices that a VPN service can operate with, which is a crucial aspect for users who need to use VPNs across various platforms and devices."&lt;SEP&gt;"The compatibility of devices with charging technology, such as Qi chargers, is discussed, showing an interest in universal charging solutions for diverse gadgets during travels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab0d5fce14fb3499b90d670996fc74d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b35bc6113a75b2108aa75e718271e05</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VPN SECURITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"VPN Security pertains to the measures and protocols a VPN employs to protect user data and privacy, such as encryption and kill switch features."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b35bc6113a75b2108aa75e718271e05</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GEOLOCATION RESTRICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Geolocation Restriction is the ability of a VPN to alter the perceived geographical location of the user's internet connection, allowing access to content restricted in certain regions and enhancing privacy while browsing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b35bc6113a75b2108aa75e718271e05</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROTOCOLS SUPPORTED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Protocols Supported indicates the various VPN protocols that a service is capable of handling, which can affect the speed and security of the VPN connection, like OpenVPN, WireGuard, or IKEv2/IPsec."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b35bc6113a75b2108aa75e718271e05</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENCRYPTION STRENGTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Encryption Strength involves the level of encryption a VPN uses to secure data transmission, often measured in terms of bits (e.g., 128-bit, 256-bit), which determines the robustness of the data protection."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b35bc6113a75b2108aa75e718271e05</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD-PARTY AUDITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Third-party Audits are security checks conducted by external organizations to verify a VPN's claims about its privacy and security measures, offering an additional layer of trust and transparency."</data>
