</node>
<node id="&quot;FDA CLEARANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"FDA clearance is a regulatory process that Apple might need to go through for advanced health features reliant on certain sensors or algorithms, particularly if they change due to patent-related design alterations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b76c81c445c4cc4d927995e223dd924</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER WEARABLES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Consumer wearables, like Apple Watch, are electronic devices designed to monitor various aspects of health and fitness, often impacted by changes in sensor technology and patent laws.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b76c81c445c4cc4d927995e223dd924</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATENT CLAIMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Patent claims are specific assertions in a patent that define the boundaries of the patent's protection, critical to the legal disputes between Apple and companies like Masimo and AliveCor.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b76c81c445c4cc4d927995e223dd924</data>
