<node id="&quot;HITOUTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hitouts are specific to Australian Rules Football and refer to the number of times a player is hit by an opponent when trying to take the ball, which is a common statistic used to gauge a player's defensive pressure and resilience."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06b83f477865b89437e1109852bb228b</data>
