  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Algorithmic content moderation refers to the use of computer algorithms to manage and filter content on social media platforms, which is a central issue in the debate regarding state laws and platform responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66c3f87316fd0396ee15a4c6ac8a46ff</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDIVIDUALIZED EXPLANATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Individualized explanations pertain to the requirement for social media platforms to provide users with reasons when their content is removed, which is a suggested obligation from state laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66c3f87316fd0396ee15a4c6ac8a46ff</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATORY CHALLENGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulatory Challenges refer to the difficulties encountered by organizations in complying with different regulatory regimes around the world, such as the challenges faced by the Wikimedia Foundation with EU regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Regulatory challenges are the difficulties and considerations surrounding the enforcement and practicality of state laws on social media platforms, particularly in relation to content moderation and the balance between free speech and the prevention of harmful content."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9519d510542618139ea10a3404f5ee70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66c3f87316fd0396ee15a4c6ac8a46ff</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUMAN MODERATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Human moderation involves the active involvement of human staff in the content moderation process, which state laws requiring individualized explanations could potentially increase due to their impact on automated systems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66c3f87316fd0396ee15a4c6ac8a46ff</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COST OF COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cost of compliance refers to the financial and logistical implications for social media companies required to adapt their content moderation systems to comply with state laws, which may include scaling up human resources or developing more sophisticated algorithms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66c3f87316fd0396ee15a4c6ac8a46ff</data>
</node>
