  <data key="d2">chunk-7850100327b1242bd027ebc775d90423</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATIONAL MUSIC PUBLISHERS ASSOCIATION (NMPA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The National Music Publishers Association is an organization representing US music publishers, involved in discussions around the regulation of AI and its impact on the creative industry."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DANIEL TENCER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Daniel Tencer is an author and contributor to Music Business Worldwide, providing commentary on entertainment events and news stories, including those related to AI in the music industry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daniel Tencer is identified as the author of the report, contributing to its creation and analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daniel Tencer is the author of the article, reporting on the issue affecting European artists and labels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d6dc2d558e8c913dc498b003e62cae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f5ee7f196a4e1405812f1ee34113944</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JKBX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"JKBX is a technology platform providing music royalties as an asset class, mentioned as a supporter of MBW Explains."&lt;SEP&gt;"JKBX is a technology platform supporting the Music Business Worldwide, focusing on providing consumers with access to music royalties."&lt;SEP&gt;"JKBX is an organization that offers a financial investment model around music, leveraging the concept of Royalty Shares for consumers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-400da07758178989d73d82b3275d9abd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-938bd4ccc5214e519143f304df98ac78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;US COPYRIGHT OFFICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The US Copyright Office is referenced in relation to copyright law, which is a governing body affecting the AI and music industry's interaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The US Copyright Office is responsible for publicizing copyright law and administering copyright registration and protection in the United States, including efforts to assess the need for legal changes regarding AI in the creative sector."&lt;SEP&gt;"US Copyright Office is the governmental body where Google filed a document concerning copyright issues, which Sony Music and other music companies are involved with in relation to AI technology."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2068f5b941dd443ab2cac507dd834dfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7228eab616f311039f5147fcaa207275</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUMAN CREATIVE CLASS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Human creative class encompasses human artists and music rights holders whose livelihoods and creative processes may be affected by the rise of AI technologies, as discussed in the context of copyright and AI regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COPYRIGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Copyright denotes the legal rights held by Globes Publisher Itonut Ltd. over the content published on December 3, 2023."&lt;SEP&gt;"Copyright is a legal concept related to the protection of creative works, with significant relevance in the discourse surrounding AI-generated content in the music industry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Copyright is the legal concept being debated in the context of AI-generated content and its implications for the music and content creation industries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2068f5b941dd443ab2cac507dd834dfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3fb89975bd79763d7ab0405adf730b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREATIVE AUTHORSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Creative authorship pertains to the rights and recognition of human creators in the creation of works, challenged by the rise of AI-generated content that may not require human authorship as traditionally defined.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC DOMAIN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public domain refers to works that are not protected by copyright and are freely available for use and distribution, a concept the NMPA suggests should relate to AI-generated content that is not copyrightable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL PURPOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commercial purpose indicates the potential use of works for commercial activities, which is a consideration in the debate over the rights and usage of AI-generated content.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DERIVATIVE WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Derivative works are new creations that are based on or incorporate aspects of existing works, relevant in the discussion of whether AI-assisted or AI-generated works can have copyright protection."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STEPHEN THALER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stephen Thaler is an individual who owns a technology, the Creativity Machine, involved in a legal case regarding AI-generated content and copyright.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREATIVITY MACHINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Creativity Machine is a technology owned by Stephen Thaler, involved in a court case about the copyrightability of AI-generated content.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;US DISTRICT COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"US District Court refers to the legal venue in Washington, D.C., where a judicial ruling regarding AI and copyright issues was made, impacting the regulation discourse on AI-generated content.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COPYRIGHTABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Copyrightability is the eligibility of a work for copyright protection, a central issue in the debate on how AI-generated content is treated under the law.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUMAN AUTHORSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Human authorship is fundamental for copyright protection, emphasized in legal discussions on AI-generated content, necessitating human involvement in the creative process.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PRECEDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Precedent refers to the potential impact of this case on future legal decisions, as it may set a standard or example for handling similar cases.&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal precedent refers to past legal decisions and interpretations that guide current and future rulings, such as the US District Court's stance on the non-copyrightability of AI-generated works without human guidance.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-057419d9dcb2bd0f16efc13c79c0ed3f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROACTIVE PROTECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Proactive protections advocate for measures to safeguard human creators prior to potential adverse effects of AI technologies, recommended by the NMPA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUMAN ARTISTRY CAMPAIGN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Human Artistry Campaign is an initiative aimed at defending human culture against potential dilution or replacement by AI technologies, aligning with concerns voiced by the NMPA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COPYRIGHT PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Copyright Protection involves the legal safeguarding of intellectual property, particularly relevant in discussions about how AI-generated content is or isn't eligible for copyright law protections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUMAN ARTISTIC EXPRESSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Human Artistic Expression pertains to the value and uniqueness of works produced by human creativity, at the heart of debates on how AI might disrupt the creative process and the value of human-created content."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AI INFRINGEMENT CONCERNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"AI Infringement Concerns relate to the potential for AI to produce content that might infringe upon existing copyrights, causing legal and ethical dilemmas within the creative industries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREATIVE INDUSTRY STAKEHOLDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Creative Industry Stakeholders include entities like Universal Music Group, musicians, and publishers, who have vested interests in the outcomes of AI interaction with creative processes and copyright laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ETHICAL AI USAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ethical AI Usage refers to the responsible incorporation of AI technologies within creative fields, ensuring they complement rather than replace human creativity and adhere to ethical standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAIR USE DOCTRINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fair Use Doctrine is a legal principle allowing limited use of copyrighted material without permission for purposes like criticism, comment, news reporting, teaching, and research, which impacts music rights usage.&lt;SEP&gt;"Fair Use Doctrine is a legal principle allowing limited use of copyrighted material without permission, relevant when considering how AI-generated content might fit within this framework."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC SENTIMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public Sentiment represents the views and opinions of the general public on AI's impact on creativity, which can influence policy and industry practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNOLOGICAL INNOVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Technological Innovation signifies the development of new technologies like AI, which poses both opportunities and challenges to established creative practices and legal norms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGISLATIVE FRAMEWORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legislative Frameworks encompass the laws and regulations developed to govern the use and implications of AI in various sectors, including the music industry, affecting how AI-related issues are addressed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL IMPACT OF AI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
