  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TALENT DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Talent Development pertains to the nurturing and honing of human skills in the face of AI advancements, emphasizing the need for training and education in areas less susceptible to automation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-343c65a2459dc13a3782c50288dd1ba1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WASHINGTON, D.C.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Washington, D.C. is the political center where legal and industry discussions regarding copyright in AI take place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Washington, D.C., marks a significant geographical location as the battleground of the Civil War and the place where Charlie Longfellow was critically injured."&lt;SEP&gt;"Washington, D.C. is where another indictment against Trump is mentioned, as a significant political location."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2b10994721c6bdb8bda9c3fe26ba47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-057419d9dcb2bd0f16efc13c79c0ed3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0f78adc782a6f418124b6487edf251</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COPYRIGHT OFFICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Copyright Office is involved in the legal discussion and decision-making process concerning copyright law and AI."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9e0f78adc782a6f418124b6487edf251</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCORD MUSIC GROUP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Concord Music Group is another key party in the music industry addressing copyright concerns regarding AI training with other industry stakeholders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9e0f78adc782a6f418124b6487edf251</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NMPA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"NMPA is an organization that is challenging the application of fair use in the context of AI development and training with copyrighted materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMPA represents music industry players and advocates for licensing requirements for AI training on copyrighted materials, opposing opt-out regimes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-400da07758178989d73d82b3275d9abd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0f78adc782a6f418124b6487edf251</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAIR USE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fair Use is a legal doctrine allowing limited use of copyrighted materials without permission, which the NMPA and UMG argue does not apply to AI training in most circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fair Use is a legal doctrine allowing the use of copyrighted material under certain conditions, which is central to the discussion on AI and copyright in the project."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fair Use refers to a legal doctrine that allows limited use of copyrighted material without permission for purposes like commentary, criticism, or news reporting; Kooker argues against its broad application in AI training.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-70761b9e90058525cd8d556a53700ac5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2068f5b941dd443ab2cac507dd834dfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0f78adc782a6f418124b6487edf251</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AI DEVELOPERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"AI Developers are entities involved in creating AI models and would be responsible for adhering to copyright laws regarding the data they use for training their algorithms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9e0f78adc782a6f418124b6487edf251</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LICENSING RECORDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Licensing Records refer to the documentation that AI developers would need to maintain as per transparency and recordkeeping requirements to prove compliance with copyright laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9e0f78adc782a6f418124b6487edf251</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSPARENCY REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transparency Requirements involve the obligation for developers to disclose their use of data, including copyrighted materials, to respect copyright laws and facilitate enforcement by rights holders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transparency Requirements mandate openness and traceability in AI technologies, a key component of the AI Act's regulation of AI applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0f78adc782a6f418124b6487edf251</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECORDKEEPING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Recordkeeping emphasizes the necessity for AI developers to maintain detailed logs of the data their AI models are trained on for legal compliance and to prove non-infringement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9e0f78adc782a6f418124b6487edf251</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COPYRIGHT INFRINGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Copyright Infringement is the unauthorized use of copyrighted materials, a central concern for the industry as AI systems increasingly utilize such content for training and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Copyright infringement refers to the illegal use of copyrighted material without permission, which is a concern within the organization as it relates to the use of datasets in AI development."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-226396bbe23d2faac70b87776260f0ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0f78adc782a6f418124b6487edf251</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COPYRIGHTED MATERIALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
