  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bon-Kyoung Koo is a researcher leading a team who discovered a critical gene in stem cell differentiation within the intestines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GABRIELE COLOZZA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gabriele Colozza is a postdoctoral researcher directing at the Center for Genome Engineering, focusing on intestinal stem cell regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMBA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"IMBA is where Bon-Kyoung Koo and his team conduct their stem cell research."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSTITUTE FOR BASIC SCIENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Institute for Basic Science is involved in collaboration with IMBA and is based in South Korea."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVYUH MEDIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Revyuh Media is the platform where the article about the research is published, categorized under business."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PANETH CELLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paneth cells are a type of secretory cells in the intestines, their proliferation influenced by Rnf43 and Daam1, and are significant in prompting cell division."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paneth cells are described as key secretory cell types that provide growth factors, influencing the stem cell population and the surrounding microenvironment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0269bd4ab428114743740d314303acbe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WNT SIGNALING PATHWAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wnt signaling pathway is a well-established mechanism in embryonic growth, and its dysregulation can cause tumor development if overstimulated."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RNF43&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rnf43 is a known regulator of the Wnt signaling pathway, initially discovered for its role in marking the Wnt receptor for destruction, and is critical in controlling stem cell differentiation in the intestines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rnf43 is implicated in the process that leads to the differentiation of stem cells into Paneth cells, affecting tumor growth when altered."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0269bd4ab428114743740d314303acbe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAAM1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Daam1 is a protein that collaborates with Rnf43 to regulate the Wnt signaling pathway, necessary for the efficient formation of Paneth cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daam1 is identified as a component associated with the non-canonical Wnt pathway, playing a critical role in the differentiation of stem cells into Paneth cells, which are key in regulating the microenvironment for stem cell survival and division."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0269bd4ab428114743740d314303acbe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTESTINAL ORGANOIDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intestinal organoids are three-dimensional cultures derived from adult stem cells that replicate the environment of the intestinal lining for research purposes, demonstrating the effects of Rnf43 and Daam1 on stem cell behavior."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TUMOR-LIKE STRUCTURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tumor-like structures refer to the abnormal growth observed in organoids when Rnf43 and Daam1 are knocked out, indicating the importance of these genes in preventing uncontrolled proliferation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STEM CELLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stem cells are mentioned as a cell type that differentiates into Paneth cells under the influence of Daam1 and Rnf43, which are critical to the intestinal environment and influence tumor growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stem cells are the focus of the research, possessing the ability to transform and renew cells, specifically within intestinal stem cells in this context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0269bd4ab428114743740d314303acbe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MECHANICAL STRESS, DIGESTIVE ENZYMES, FLUCTUATING PH LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ENVIRONMENTAL FACTORS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are the extreme conditions faced by cells in the intestines, to which stem cells must adapt and respond to maintain tissue health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCONTROLLED STEM CELL PROLIFERATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Uncontrolled stem cell proliferation refers to the potential for stem cells to contribute to tumor formation if they multiply unchecked."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4800bbb22fb7af5b59deeac79e8d4dd2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TUMOR CELLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tumor cells are discussed in the context of modifying their microenvironment to facilitate their own growth, suggesting a complex interaction with surrounding cells.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0269bd4ab428114743740d314303acbe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTESTINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The intestine is mentioned as a context where the natural balance of Paneth cells influences stem cell behavior, contrasting with organoid culture conditions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0269bd4ab428114743740d314303acbe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wnt is a signaling pathway involved in cell differentiation and is provided by Paneth cells to support stem cell survival and division in the intestine."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0269bd4ab428114743740d314303acbe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEAN HOLLISTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sean Hollister is an author and journalist covering technology news for The Verge."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sean Hollister is the author of the article, likely involved in journalism or writing for The Verge."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b5f3c79911cd9857a69ceaa748a8028&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82ef6612b6aebc4c34f55e1e050f5dad</data>
</node>
