  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OLDER PEOPLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Older people, who are more susceptible to Alzheimer's due to aging changes, are a demographic that can potentially benefit from sustainable and safer nutrition strategies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ALZHEIMER'S DISEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Alzheimer's disease is a neurodegenerative condition affecting millions of Americans, highlighting the urgency for research in disease prevention and management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSTAINABLE AND SAFER NUTRITION STRATEGIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sustainable and safer nutrition strategies refer to dietary approaches that are tailored to maintain health and enhance safety, particularly beneficial for older individuals with aging metabolisms that may be more vulnerable to neurodegenerative conditions like Alzheimer's disease."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRAIN HEALTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Brain health encapsulates the overall well-being of the brain, encompassing various aspects such as cognitive performance, neuroinflammation, and the presence of new neurons, which are critical in understanding the impact of fasting-mimicking diets and intermittent fasting on aging and disease prevention."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEUROINFLAMMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Neuroinflammation is a pathological process in the brain that is associated with aging and neurodegenerative diseases, including Alzheimer's, and is targeted by fasting-mimicking diets and intermittent fasting to reduce risk factors and promote brain health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPEROXIDE PRODUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Superoxide production is a type of oxidative stress within the brain that can lead to cellular damage and aging, which fasting-mimicking diets aim to reduce in their beneficial effects against aging and disease risk factors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAKY GUT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leaky gut is a condition where the intestinal lining becomes more permeable than normal, which can allow bacteria and toxins to pass into the bloodstream, potentially leading to inflammation and exacerbating brain health issues. Intermittent fasting may help to repair and improve gut health, thereby indirectly benefiting brain health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KETOSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ketosis is a metabolic state induced by the ketogenic diet, where the body switches from using carbohydrates to fat as an energy source, producing ketones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ketosis is a metabolic state where the body utilizes fat for energy instead of glucose, which has been associated with beneficial cognitive effects. Fasting-mimicking diets can induce higher levels of ketosis, which is advantageous for brain function and potentially mitigates some symptoms associated with neurodegenerative diseases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78c1f2b5c8f3560d06e373c8068c9452</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIME-RESTRICTED EATING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Time-restricted eating is an eating pattern that restricts food intake to certain hours of the day, which can improve sleep quality and lead to better brain recovery. It is suggested to have cognitive and health benefits, including improved management of blood sugar levels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROLONGED FASTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Prolonged fasting refers to extended periods without food intake, which can trigger cellular processes like autophagy, potentially offering protective effects against neurodegenerative diseases such as Alzheimer's by recycling damaged cellular components and aiding in overall brain health maintenance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTOPHAGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Autophagy is a cellular recycling process that removes waste and damaged components. It is a crucial mechanism that supports cellular health and longevity, and during fasting, it plays a significant role in protecting the brain from diseases like Alzheimer's by cleaning out damaged cells and supporting the body's repair systems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d71f5203110cdf0ffe66b7c70dfc3ac2</data>
</node>
