  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CANNES MUSIC FESTIVAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cannes Music Festival is an international event celebrating music and artists, where discussions on industry standards and rights may take place."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GLOBAL MUSIC RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Global Music Rights is an organization that works to ensure proper music licensing and royalties for songwriters and publishers globally."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREATIVE COMMONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Creative Commons is a nonprofit organization that provides free legal tools allowing creators to grant certain usage rights to the public to their creative work, which can impact music distribution and rights.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMUSIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"eMusic is a digital music service provider that connects independent labels and artists with consumers, influencing music distribution and rights issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL MILLENNIUM COPYRIGHT ACT (DMCA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Digital Millennium Copyright Act (DMCA) is a U.S. law that implements international treaties on copyright and addresses digital rights management and copyright infringement issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BROADCAST LICENSING EXCHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Broadcast Licensing Exchange is a system used by broadcasters to license music for television and radio broadcasts, which affects how sound recordings are licensed and monetized.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MUSIC LICENSING AND COLLECTIVE MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Music Licensing and Collective Management refers to the legal and organizational process of obtaining rights to music for public performance and distribution, crucial for protecting artists’ and rights holders' interests."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECORDING INDUSTRY ASSOCIATION OF AMERICA (RIAA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Recording Industry Association of America (RIAA) is a trade organization of the United States recorded music industry, involved in protecting music copyright and distribution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOUNDEXCHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"SoundExchange is an organization that collects and distributes digital performance royalties for sound recordings used in broadcasting, particularly in public radio and television.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERFORMING RIGHTS ORGANIZATIONS (PROS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Performing Rights Organizations (PROs) are entities that collect royalties on behalf of songwriters and publishers when their music is publicly performed, a key element in music licensing.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATIONAL MUSIC PUBLISHERS’ ASSOCIATION (NMPA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"National Music Publishers’ Association (NMPA) is an American trade association that represents music publishers, songwriters, and artists regarding their interests in music publishing and copyright.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMERICAN SOCIETY OF COMPOSERS, AUTHORS AND PUBLISHERS (ASCAP)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"American Society of Composers, Authors and Publishers (ASCAP) is a non-profit performance rights organization that ensures songwriters and publishers are compensated for the use of their music.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIETY OF EUROPEAN STAGE AUTHORS AND COMPOSERS (SESAC)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Society of European Stage Authors and Composers (SESAC) represents creators and publishers in Europe, ensuring copyright protection and compensation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MERLIN RIGHTS CLEARANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Merlin Rights Clearance is a service that connects music users with publishers and rights holders to clear the necessary music licenses for a project.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREATIVE COMMONS LICENSE (CCL)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Creative Commons License (CCL) offers various licenses that creators can choose to apply to their work, impacting how it is used and shared by the public.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPACT OF TECHNOLOGY ON MUSIC INDUSTRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Impact of Technology on Music Industry is a broad concept addressing how technological advancements affect music creation, distribution, and rights management.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MUSIC PIRACY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Music Piracy refers to the illegal copying and distribution of music, which poses challenges to copyright and revenue generation in the music industry.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL SINGLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Digital Single is a term for a song released in a digital format, representing a modern method of music consumption and distribution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINSTREAM MUSIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mainstream Music typically refers to music that is widely popular and accessible to a broad audience, often impacting performance rights and licensing.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOCAL MUSIC SCENE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Local Music Scene represents the grassroots level of music production and distribution, which can be affected by copyright and licensing regulations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SYNDICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Syndication involves the sale or licensing of music to multiple broadcasters or platforms, affecting how music is distributed and rights are managed.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MUSICIANS’ GUILD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Musicians’ Guild is an organization that likely represents and protects the interests of musicians, including their copyright and rights to their performances.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSFER OF RIGHTS AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transfer of Rights Agreement is a legal document that outlines the terms under which copyright and related rights are transferred, critical for music publishing and licensing.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;USAGE RIGHTS MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Usage Rights Management involves the administration and enforcement of rights related to music usage, an integral part of copyright management in the music industry.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COPYRIGHT LAW AMENDMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Copyright Law Amendments are legislative changes that impact how music copyright is managed, protecting and evolving with the changing musical landscape.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIVE PERFORMANCE ROYALTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Live Performance Royalties are payments made to artists for live performances, a component of the overall compensation for musicians' work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECORDING STUDIO OWNERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Recording Studio Ownership pertains to the rights and management of recording facilities, which can have legal and financial implications for music production.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MUSIC SAMPLING RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Music Sampling Rights concern the permissions needed to use portions of copyrighted music in new compositions, a legal aspect of music production and distribution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTENDED PLAY (EP)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Extended Play (EP) is a musical recording longer than a single but shorter than an album, with implications for music consumption and copyright.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPILATION ALBUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compilation Album is a collection of tracks from various artists or periods, relevant for copyright considerations and music distribution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISTRIBUTION RIGHTS AGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Distribution Rights Agency likely handles the rights related to distributing music across various platforms and territories, influencing how music reaches the public.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATIONAL ENDOWMENT FOR THE ARTS (NEA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"National Endowment for the Arts (NEA) is an American institution that funds, strengthens, and projects excellence in the arts, which could be indirectly related to the music industry through arts funding and support.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EQUITY VS. ROYALTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Equity vs. Royalties concerns the financial arrangements and benefits for musicians, with equity representing ownership stakes and royalties referring to payment based on music sales or use.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MUSIC EDUCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Music Education encompasses teaching and learning about music, which can intersect with the legal aspects of music through copyright and performance rights.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CULTURAL IMPACT OF MUSIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cultural Impact of Music addresses how music influences and reflects cultures, an area that may intersect with music industry practices and regulations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOVERNMENT MUSIC POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Government Music Policy refers to laws and regulations enacted by governments that affect the music industry, including copyright and distribution practices.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTIST REPRESENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Artist Representation involves professionals or entities that manage and negotiate on behalf of artists' contracts and rights, crucial for legal and business aspects in the music industry.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MUSIC ROYALTIES CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Music Royalties Calculation is the method by which royalties are determined and distributed to rights holders, fundamental for understanding music industry economics.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVERSITY IN MUSIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Diversity in Music highlights the importance of varied cultural representations and inclusivity within the music industry, which may relate to copyright and licensing considerations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05f30bb173fe6db60e7dcd8827ab3372</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
