  <data key="d1">"Hope is a cricketer who played a pivotal role in his team's innings, contributing 43 runs in 43 balls to help avoid defeat.&lt;SEP&gt;"Hope is a researcher studying the mechanisms behind HIV infections in a lab setting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;62 FOR THREE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"62 for three is a cricketing milestone, where a team has scored 62 runs without losing their three wickets in the process, it's a significant achievement in an innings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATCH PERFORMANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Match Performance refers to the overall execution and strategy employed by both teams during the cricket match, which includes batting, bowling, fielding, and critical moments that influence the game's result."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BATTING STRATEGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Batting Strategy encompasses the tactics and decisions made by a cricket team regarding the order of batsmen, aggressive or conservative play, and adapting to the opposing team's bowlers and field placements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPPOSITION ANALYSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Opposition Analysis involves studying the weaknesses, strengths, and patterns of the opposing team's batting, bowling, and fielding, which can lead to strategic advantages in the match."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIELDING COORDINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fielding Coordination pertains to the teamwork and positioning of fielders on the cricket field, aiming to prevent runs and create opportunities for wickets, an essential aspect of an effective defensive and attacking cricket strategy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SQUAD MORALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Squad Morale reflects the psychological and emotional state of the players, which can affect their performance and impact the team's dynamics and overall success on the field."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PITCH CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pitch Conditions refer to how the playing surface, including factors like grass length, wear, and dew, can significantly affect the gameplay, especially the behavior of the ball and its movement off the pitch."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPIN BOWLING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Spin Bowling is a cricket bowling technique where the ball is turned or spinning, causing it to deviate from a straight path after pitching. It is a crucial strategy often employed to deceive batsmen and create bowling variations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BALL SPEED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ball Speed is a critical attribute of bowling that can affect batsmen's timing and ability to play shots, as well as the trajectory and bounce of the ball upon pitching.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WICKET PRESERVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GOAL"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wicket Preservation is a bowling strategy aimed at maintaining the wicket by taking wickets and minimizing extras, which is essential to build pressure and maintain an advantage in limited-overs cricket matches.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TACTICAL RETREAT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tactical Retreat is a bowling tactic where bowlers move back slightly after the initial length delivery, which can confuse the batsmen and lead to taking wickets or losing their wickets more easily.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNINGS MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innings Management involves the tactical decisions around when to declare an innings, bowl powerplays, and manage the run rate, crucial for teams playing limited-overs cricket formats to reach their target within the given number of overs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BALL-BY-BALL ANALYSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ball-by-Ball Analysis is the methodical breakdown of each delivery's impact during a match, assessing edges, bounces, and field placements to make real-time strategic decisions and adjustments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CROWD INFLUENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Crowd Influence involves the psychological effect of the audience and the atmosphere of the crowd on the players and the game, which can sometimes influence the players' performances and decisions on the field.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BAT-TOSS DYNAMICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bat-Toss Dynamics are related to the process and decisions involved in changing the bowler, which can be a strategic move to surprise the batsmen or exploit a specific weakness.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CATCHING SKILLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Catching Skills encompass the ability and practice of fielders to catch and retrieve the ball effectively, a vital defensive component in cricket that can lead to dismissals and momentum shifts.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSISTENT PERFORMANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GOAL"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Consistent Performance highlights the importance of maintaining a high standard of play throughout the match, which can be a determinant of the team's success in cricket.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRESSURE SITUATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pressure Situations are moments of intense stress during the game, such as close calls or late-stage fielding chances, that can test a team's composure and decision-making under pressure.&lt;SEP&gt;"Pressure situations refer to the intense conditions under which NASCAR drivers and teams must perform, requiring exceptional composure and response."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-296311b5d203432895ff6e0493c7b788&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;END-OF-INNINGS DISCUSSIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"End-of-Innings Discussions are deliberations among cricket captains or selectors before the completion of the match that can influence team's strategies for future games.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLAYER ROTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Player Rotation is the strategy of rotating players to manage their fatigue, maintain fitness, and ensure player participation, crucial for long cricket seasons and tournaments.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SLIP FIELDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Slip Fielders are fielders positioned behind the batsman, particularly on the off side, who are responsible for catching edges hit by the batsman, a key position for catching opportunities and run-outs.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SQUARE LEG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Square Leg is another fielding position, strategically placed behind the batsman to catch edges on the on side, complementing the slip fielders and providing additional coverage.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MOMENTUM SWINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Momentum Swings describe instances in the match where a small advantage or event creates a ripple effect, influencing the team's morale, psychological state, and subsequent performance either positively or negatively.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CROWD ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Crowd Engagement involves the interaction between the spectators and the on-field action, which can energize players and affect their performance in a cricket match.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPIRIT OF CRICKET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Spirit of Cricket embodies the principles of fairness, respect, sportsmanship, and play for enjoyment, which are fundamental to the ethos and integrity of the game."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIELD MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Field Management refers to the strategic positioning and movement of fielders during the game to cover potential hitting zones and outfield movement to minimize runs and maximize defensive effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EDGE CATCHING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Edge Catching is a defensive fielding strategy where fielders aim to catch edges hit off the bat or glove, which can result in outs and wickets.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BATTING STROKES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Batting Strokes involve the various techniques and shots batsmen use to score runs, including drives, pulls, and flicks, which are crucial for building partnerships and exerting pressure on the opposition bowlers.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOSS ADVANTAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Toss Advantage relates to the captains' decision on whether to bat or field first based on the ball's likely behavior after being bowled, a strategic choice that can provide a significant edge in limited-overs cricket formats.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BOWLER SURVIVABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GOAL"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bowler Survivability refers to the ability of a bowlers to remain fit and effective throughout the match or innings, a critical aspect of maintaining a competitive bowling lineup.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FASTEST TEMPO BATTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fastest Tempo Batting is a batting strategy adopted by some players to score runs at a rapid pace, taking advantage of gaps in the fielding or bowling. It can be particularly effective in limited-overs formats where the batting team has a large target to chase.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WICKET TROUBLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wicket Trouble denotes a situation where a batsman is frequently dismissed, often due to bowling actions targeting their weaknesses or errors, putting pressure on the team's batting lineup.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DUAL BATTING STRATEGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dual Batting Strategy involves having two key batsmen accustomed to facing specific bowling attacks, ensuring that each can handle different types of bowlers effectively, thereby strengthening the team's overall batting resilience.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURSE OF PLAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Course of Play refers to the sequence of events and strategic decisions that unfold during a cricket match, shaping the game's dynamics and affecting the teams' performances.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLOATING STRIKERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Floating Strikers signifies batsmen who adopt a deceptive and unpredictable approach to scoring runs, making it difficult for fielders to time their shots and increases the likelihood of scoring."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EDGE PLAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Edge Play is a specialized fielding technique where fielders aim to catch edges hit off the bat or glove, often aiming for quick take-ons to create pressure or potential wickets.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DECISION-MAKING UNDER PRESSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Decision-Making Under Pressure involves the cognitive processes and mental resilience that players exhibit when facing high-stress situations, such as close calls or critical moments in the match.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRITICAL HIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Critical Hit is a decisive move or shot that can turn the game's momentum, often involving a boundary or a six scored due to advantageous conditions or skillful execution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LINE AND LEG-BEFORE-WICKET (LBW)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"RULE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LBW is a cricketing rule where a batter is out if the ball pitches on or leg side of them without being struck by the bat, a vital part of batting defense and umpire decisions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNINGS DISPATCH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innings Dispatch refers to the act of dismissing a batsman, which can shift the game's scoreboard and alter momentum, a frequent occurrence in cricket.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BATTING PARTNERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Batting Partnership refers to the collaboration between two batsmen, which can strengthen their line-up, provide stability, and exert pressure on the opposing team's bowlers and fielders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POWERPLAY OPPORTUNITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Powerplay Opportunities are periods during limited-overs cricket when extra fielders are allowed, encouraging aggressive batting to chase a lower target in fewer overs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRATEGIC TIMING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Strategic Timing involves the batsman's choice of when to play shots, based on factors like field positioning, bowler's strategy, and scoreboard pressure, to maximize scoring and defensive effectiveness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Strategic Timing relates to the timing of the national team's games and travel, which is a point of debate in the context of readiness for the Euros."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04be473f3997f28a85c65e480511c660&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAPTAINCY WISDOM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Captaincy Wisdom pertains to the leadership qualities, strategic insight, and decision-making prowess of a cricket team's captain, which can greatly influence the team's performance and morale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRICKETING AMBIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cricketing Ambiance describes the atmosphere and mood on a cricket field, including crowd noise, weather conditions, and general spectator engagement, which can influence player performance and the overall experience of the sport."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLAYER EXCELLENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GOAL"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Player Excellence highlights extraordinary individual skills or performances that stand out and elevate the standard of play within a team and contribute to the team's success and reputation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RUN EQUATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Run Equation involves the calculation and tactical use of runs scored to maximize a team's chance of victory in a cricket match, crucial in limited-overs formats where scoring targets are fixed.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODIFIED BOWLING TACTICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Modified Bowling Tactics refer to the adjustments made by bowlers in response to changes in match conditions, player performances, or batting strategies, to maintain or gain an advantage for their team."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCONVENTIONAL FIELDING PLACEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Unconventional Fielding Placements are strategic decisions to position fielders in non-standard positions, often aiming to create surprises or exploit specific batting techniques or errors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DYNAMIC BOWL ROTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dynamic Bowl Rotation denotes the practice of changing bowlers frequently and intelligently throughout the match to confuse the opposition and maintain adaptability to batting strategies, especially useful in long-format cricket matches that can span several days.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENSEMBLE TEAMWORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ensemble Teamwork emphasizes the collaborative effort and mutual support among team members, contributing to effective performance across various aspects like batting, bowling, and fielding in cricket."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLAYER UNDERTAKING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Player Undertaking refers to the commitment and personal growth of individual players, taking on challenges, and aiming for excellence within the team's competitive framework."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BROADCAST COMMENTARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTEXT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Broadcast Commentary refers to the analysis and opinions provided by commentators during a cricket match, which can shape public perception and provide insights into the game for viewers at home and players on the field."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WICKET DRUMMING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"HUMOROUS EXPRESSION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wicket Drumming humorously describes fielders rhythmically tapping the ground while waiting for a ball, indicating impatience or anxiety for a potential catch, a popular depiction in cricket narratives."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPPOSITION'S GRATITUDE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Opposition's Gratitude might humorously suggest a scenario where the opposing team, upon defeat, shows appreciation for the skillful play or fairness displayed by the losing team, reflecting sportsmanship and camaraderie in cricket.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVIVAL CHANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SPORTSMANSHIP"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Revival Chant could be a make-believe expression representing a team or fans' motivational chant, expressing their determination to come back stronger after a loss, a sentiment often shared among cricket enthusiasts.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BATTING SYMPHONY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"METAPHOR"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Batting Symphony is a metaphorical expression that implies the team batters working in harmony, akin to musicians in an orchestra, playing their shots with precision and coordination for maximum effectiveness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPPORTIVE NOISE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Supportive Noise captures the background commentary or crowd reactions that bolster the morale and determination during a cricket match, symbolizing collective support for the players' efforts on the field.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SENSATION SEEKING BATSMAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sensation Seeking Batsman denotes a cricketer attracted to taking high-risk shots for the thrill and the potential of scoring quickly, often leading to notable moments in the game."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6aab93b76cb61672534ca832d942902f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCTOBER 2, 2023&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"October 2, 2023 is the date the article was published, marking the event of its release."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text was published on October 2, 2023, providing a temporal context for the information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5774b26ddfa61c3150551bd35832271b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fa83179c1c7eaf784f471825720c37</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NBA BETTING SITES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"NBA Betting Sites are online platforms where users can place bets on NBA MVP futures and other sports-related events."&lt;SEP&gt;"NBA betting sites are platforms where individuals can place bets on NBA games and events, offering prop bets among other betting options."&lt;SEP&gt;"NBA betting sites are where bettors place wagers on NBA games, and the user is seeking advice on what to look for."&lt;SEP&gt;"NBA betting sites refer to the online platforms used to place bets on NBA games, which is the technology in question for sports betting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5774b26ddfa61c3150551bd35832271b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fa83179c1c7eaf784f471825720c37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c671083ad83b289daa2fec521ad6c448&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ed5b7940a905a326304c1667738a001</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DRAFTKINGS SPORTSBOOK PROMOTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"DraftKings Sportsbook promotions refer to special offers and deals provided by the company for its customers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5774b26ddfa61c3150551bd35832271b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FANDUEL PROMOTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"FanDuel promotions refer to specific offers and benefits provided by FanDuel Sportsbook to its customers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5774b26ddfa61c3150551bd35832271b</data>
</node>
