</node>
<node id="&quot;CAMBRIAN EXPLOSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Cambrian explosion was a period of rapid diversification in life forms, including the emergence of complex multicellular organisms and groups such as mollusks and crustaceans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GONDWANA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gondwana was a supercontinent that played a role in the Earth's geological and climatic history, influencing the distribution and evolution of life."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORDOVICIAN MASS EXTINCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Ordovician mass extinction was a significant event where half of all existing genuses perished, affecting marine and early terrestrial life forms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMIAN PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERIOD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Permian period was a span of geological time that included the Great Dying, the most severe extinction event in Earth's history."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GREAT DYING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Great Dying, also known as the Permian-Triassic extinction, saw the disappearance of approximately 90% of all species, particularly impacting marine organisms, early fish species, and many land-dwelling amphibians and reptiles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRILOBITES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Trilobites were marine arthropods that became extinct during the Great Dying, representing a significant loss in prehistoric life forms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEGANEUROPSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Meganeuropsis is a genus of giant dragonfly that is often depicted in art from the Carboniferous period and represents a species that went extinct during the Great Dying."&lt;SEP&gt;"Meganeuropsis is a large dragonfly from the Carboniferous period, often depicted in art, representing an extinct species that has left a lasting impact on people's imaginations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PALEOZOIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ERA"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Paleozoic is an era in Earth's geological timescale, marked by the Cambrian explosion and significant biodiversity, starting around 540 million years ago and ending 251 million years ago."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRATOSPHERIC OZONE LAYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The stratospheric ozone layer, which developed during the Neoproterozoic era, protected Earth's surface from ultraviolet radiation and allowed for the colonization of land by animals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHEMICAL WEATHERING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chemical weathering refers to the breakdown of rocks, soil, and minerals through chemical reactions, which can influence climate by affecting atmospheric CO2 levels and contribute to cooling effects, as seen after the Ordovician mass extinction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VOLCANIC EMISSIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Volcanic emissions release gases and CO2 into the atmosphere, contributing to warming and cooling events depending on their interaction with other Earth systems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC CO2 LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Atmospheric CO2 levels are a critical factor in Earth's climate, influencing global temperatures, glacial cycles, and mass extinctions through greenhouse effects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;P-T EXTINCTION EVENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"P-T extinction event is a significant event marking the boundary between the Paleozoic and Mesozoic eras, leading to massive die-offs and ecological shifts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANTS WITH ROOTS, STEMS, AND LEAVES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Plants that emerged midway through the Paleozoic with roots, stems, and leaves played a role in chemical weathering, affecting CO2 levels and ecological dynamics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SYNAPSIDS AND THERAPSIDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Synapsids and therapsids are groups of early terrestrial animals that existed before and during the P-T extinction event, with various members evolving into mammals and dinosaurs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CYNODONTIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cynodontia is a group of proto-mammals, ancestors of modern mammals, that thrived in the Triassic period, adapting by shrinking in size to evade reptilian predators."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARCHOSAURS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Archosaurs are a subgroup of synapsids that developed a more efficient respiratory system, enabling them to better utilize oxygen during the P-T extinction event, aiding their rise to dominance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINENTAL DRIFT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Continental drift is a slow movement of Earth's continents over the globe, which over millions of years has significantly altered the planet's geological and climatic conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PANGEA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LANDMASS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pangea was a supercontinent that existed during the late Paleozoic and early Mesozoic eras, bringing all landmasses together before breaking apart into the continents we know today."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLIMATE MODEL SIMULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SCIENTIFIC METHOD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Climate model simulations are computational tools used by scientists to replicate and understand past, present, and future climate patterns based on various parameters and greenhouse gas concentrations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOSSIL RIVER DEPOSITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEOLOGICAL EVIDENCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fossil river deposits provide geological evidence of past environments and can give insights into the Earth's climate, such as the conditions during the Permian period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARINE FOOD WEB&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL STRUCTURE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The marine food web refers to the complex network of interdependent marine organisms, which was disrupted in the late Permian, possibly contributing to low oxygen levels in the atmosphere."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC OXYGEN LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL MEASUREMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Atmospheric oxygen levels are a critical chemical measurement indicating the concentration of oxygen in the Earth's atmosphere, which has fluctuated greatly over geological timescales and has significant implications for life on Earth."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8cb6655fd17d00c0d51e7fddac5d774</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RODENT OF UNUSUAL SIZE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rodent of Unusual Size is an extinct prehistoric creature that grew very large during the Triassic period but later shrunk in size to that of modern-day field mice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a7d1428dd177c265ee0f8475f062a06c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRIASSIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERIOD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Triassic is a geological period during Earth's history when the Rodent of Unusual Size lived and grew to enormous sizes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a7d1428dd177c265ee0f8475f062a06c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODERN-DAY FIELD MICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"modern-day field mice are the descendants of the Rodent of Unusual Size, now living at a much smaller size."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a7d1428dd177c265ee0f8475f062a06c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPTILIAN PREDATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Reptilian predators refer to the reptiles that preyed upon the Rodent of Unusual Size during the Triassic period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a7d1428dd177c265ee0f8475f062a06c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREDATORY REPTILES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Predatory reptiles are the class of reptiles that were predators to the Rodent of Unusual Size during the Triassic period, playing a crucial role in its environmental pressure and size adaptation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a7d1428dd177c265ee0f8475f062a06c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADAPTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adaptation refers to the evolutionary process through which the Rodent of Unusual Size became smaller in size to evade predators, specifically the reptilian predators during the Triassic period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a7d1428dd177c265ee0f8475f062a06c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;10 MINUTE SCHOOL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"10 Minute School is an edtech company in Bangladesh aiming to democratize education and provide supplementary learning resources for K12 students."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AYMAN SADIQ&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ayman Sadiq is the co-founder of 10 Minute School and was previously a teacher at a coaching center in Dhaka. He initiated the project to address the challenges faced by students in rural areas, particularly the high cost of tuition and travel to Dhaka for education."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BANGLADESH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bangladesh is the country where 10 Minute School operates and seeks to provide educational opportunities to a large student base with challenges in rural areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bangladesh is the market where a new educational venture is being introduced."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59c722edb7d9681b25974c55aed34c09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONJUNCTION CAPITAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conjunction Capital is a private investor that led the funding round for 10 Minute School, showing interest in the potential to redefine the education landscape in Bangladesh."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conjunction Capital is an investment managing partner firm making statements about their ventures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59c722edb7d9681b25974c55aed34c09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PEAK XV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Peak XV, formerly known as Sequoia Capital India, is a participating investor in the funding round for 10 Minute School, contributing to its growth."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STARTUP BANGLADESH LIMITED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Startup Bangladesh Limited, the Bangladesh government's sovereign venture fund, is also an investor in 10 Minute School, indicating government support for the edtech initiative."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KUNAL SHAH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Kunal Shah is the CEO of CRED and a participating investor in the funding round for 10 Minute School, highlighting the involvement of educational and tech industry leaders in the company's expansion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAJID RAHMAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sajid Rahman is the managing partner of MyAsiaVC and a participating investor in the funding round for 10 Minute School, signifying support from experienced venture capitalists."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TELECOM OPERATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Telecom operators are among the sponsors that supported the 10 Minute School YouTube channel, indicating their interest in educational content and technology."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELECTRONICS COMPANIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Electronics companies are among the sponsors that provided funding for the 10 Minute School, involved in supporting educational technology initiatives."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FMCG BRANDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"FMCG brands participated as sponsors in the creation of educational content, showing corporate investment in edtech for societal impact."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;K12 STUDENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DEMOGRAPHIC"</data>
  <data key="d1">"K12 students are the target demographic for 10 Minute School's educational resources, highlighting the platform's focus on providing learning materials for this age group."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RURAL AND SEMI-URBAN AREAS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DEMOGRAPHIC"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rural and semi-urban areas are mentioned as regions where 52% of 10 Minute School's students come from, indicating the platform's reach to underserved communities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRADES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EDUCATIONAL LEVEL"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Grades refer to the range of schooling stages (K12) that 10 Minute School targets with its educational content.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELEMENTARY SCHOOL LEARNERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DEMOGRAPHIC"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Elementary school learners are noted as competitors to 10 Minute School, indicating the market segment for primary education technology solutions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MYASIAVC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"MyAsiaVC is a venture capital firm that participated in the funding of 10 Minute School, showing a focus on investment in Asian edtech companies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;42 MILLION STUDENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STATISTIC"</data>
  <data key="d1">"42 million students represent the total enrollment in the K12 system in Bangladesh, indicating the scale of the educational challenge that 10 Minute School is addressing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;QUALITY TEACHERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"RESOURCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Quality teachers are mentioned as a lacking resource in areas outside the capital city, which is a key issue that edtech like 10 Minute School is trying to address."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AFFORDABLE MANNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Affordable manner refers to the strategy of making quality education accessible through technology for those who cannot afford traditional methods or live outside major educational hubs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ef95606b02ac0381b175c0cc21ec878</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KIRILL KOZHEVNIKOV&quot;">
