</node>
<node id="&quot;HYDROTHERMAL VENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hydrothermal vents are locations in the deep sea where chemosynthesis occurs, supporting life and expanding our understanding of habitable conditions beyond sunlight-dependent ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrothermal vents are specific environments in the deep sea that Jon Copley has studied, and are noted for their unique ecosystem and vulnerability due to their limited area and species exclusivity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrothermal vents are specific environments in the deep sea that Jon Copley has studied, noted for their unique ecosystem and vulnerability due to their limited area and species exclusivity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4feba597c2dd25bbb78301549e87548c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEEP SEA ANIMALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Deep sea animals are the inhabitants of the deep sea that Copley's research focuses on, including their interactions and adaptations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4feba597c2dd25bbb78301549e87548c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SENSORY ECOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sensory ecology is a specific area within deep sea research that Jon Copley mentions, dealing with how deep sea creatures perceive and interact with their environment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4feba597c2dd25bbb78301549e87548c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OXYGEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Oxygen is a critical element for deep sea animals, its levels and distribution being a significant point of discussion in relation to the effects of climate change."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a critical element for deep sea life, its levels and distribution being a significant point of discussion in relation to the effects of climate change."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is essential for deep sea animals and is carried down by currents from polar regions to the deep ocean."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4feba597c2dd25bbb78301549e87548c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POLAR REGIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Polar Regions are the areas where auroras, such as Northern and Southern Lights, are typically visible due to the magnetic field configuration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polar regions are the source of currents that carry oxygen to the deep ocean, which is crucial for sustaining deep sea life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polar regions are where the currents form that carry oxygen to the deep sea, and are mentioned in the context of climate change's effect on the ocean's ability to transport oxygen."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a6f066c91f364f8cef4b14857a3fc634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4feba597c2dd25bbb78301549e87548c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEAWATER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Seawater is essential for deep sea life, as it carries oxygen and is the medium in which hydrothermal vents and other deep sea ecosystems exist. It's also mentioned in the context of climate change impacts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seawater is essential for deep sea life, its role as a carrier of oxygen and habitat for deep sea ecosystems, is discussed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4feba597c2dd25bbb78301549e87548c</data>
</node>
