<node id="&quot;FANDOM COMMUNITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fandom communities are groups of individuals who share a common interest in a particular artist or band, often relying on experiences like live concerts and concert films to foster a sense of identity and belonging."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-835769d53ba2905e28aedb8687e3ca91</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCESSIBILITY CHALLENGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Accessibility challenges include geographical, economic, health, and safety considerations that can prevent fans from attending live events, leading to a greater reliance on concert films and other accessible alternatives."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-835769d53ba2905e28aedb8687e3ca91</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FANDOM CULTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fandom culture refers to the activities, communities, and collective experiences of fans regarding their shared enthusiasm for an artist or group, highlighting the social aspect and sense of belonging it provides."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6a6677081ba1bf7c665602ed9182e88a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STADIUM AND ARENA CONCERTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stadium and Arena Concerts are large-scale live performances by popular musical artists that often take place in significant venues, sometimes creating a hierarchy of experience based on attendance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6a6677081ba1bf7c665602ed9182e88a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ATTENDANCE BARRIERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Attendance barriers refer to the obstacles that may prevent fans from experiencing live music events in person, such as geographical distance, financial constraints, and social stigmas."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6a6677081ba1bf7c665602ed9182e88a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEVERAGING TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leveraging technology in the context of music refers to the use of digital platforms, like concert films, to overcome traditional barriers and facilitate fan engagement with musical artists and performances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6a6677081ba1bf7c665602ed9182e88a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAN HIERARCHY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fan hierarchy is an informal structure that may emerge within fan communities, often based on factors such as perceived devotion, ability to attend major events, or possess additional merchandise or memorabilia."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6a6677081ba1bf7c665602ed9182e88a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAN PRIVILEGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fan privilege denotes the advantages some fans have, such as greater access to events, exclusive experiences, or the means to travel, often due to socioeconomic status or geographical location."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6a6677081ba1bf7c665602ed9182e88a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YLVA JOHANSSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ylva Johansson is the European Union’s home affairs commissioner, involved in a controversy regarding a microtargeted political ad campaign."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-674db37cf38da4f0619869a8020ebf71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT'S LIBE COMMITTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The European Parliament’s LIBE committee is involved in discussing and pressing for details about the ad campaign."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-674db37cf38da4f0619869a8020ebf71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"MEPs are members of the European Parliament pressing for answers and clarifications from the Commission."&lt;SEP&gt;"MEPs are members of the European Parliament, involved in pressing for details and accountability regarding the microtargeted ad campaign."&lt;SEP&gt;"MEPs stands for Members of the European Parliament, the elected body of the European Union that participates in the legislative process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-674db37cf38da4f0619869a8020ebf71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DANNY MEKIĆ&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Danny Mekić is a technologist who discovered and reported on the microtargeted ad campaign, playing a role in the uncovering of the situation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-674db37cf38da4f0619869a8020ebf71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DE VOLKSKRANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"De Volkskrant is a Dutch newspaper where Mekić published his findings on the microtargeted ad campaign, contributing to the public availability of information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-674db37cf38da4f0619869a8020ebf71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YOUGOV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"RESEARCH FIRM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"YouGov is a research firm that conducted surveys indicating low support for the CSAM-scanning proposal among the European population, contradicting the ad campaign's implications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-674db37cf38da4f0619869a8020ebf71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOVUS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"RESEARCH FIRM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Novus, like YouGov, conducted surveys that indicated little support for the CSAM-scanning proposal among Europeans, contributing to the fact-checking process against the ad campaign's claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-674db37cf38da4f0619869a8020ebf71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JULIAN ASSANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Julian Assange is mentioned as an interest point related to privacy, which was seemingly an exclusion criterion in the ad's microtargeting strategy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-674db37cf38da4f0619869a8020ebf71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEXIT&quot;, &quot;BREXIT&quot;, &quot;SPANEXIT&quot;, &quot;AFD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These terms are related to political groups and events that by being excluded, suggest a bias in the ad campaign's microtargeting strategy, which could be a point of contention regarding the fairness and transparency of the campaign."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-674db37cf38da4f0619869a8020ebf71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHRISTIANITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Christianity was explicitly excluded from the microtargeting, which is relevant to the discussion on fairness and transparency in political ad targeting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-674db37cf38da4f0619869a8020ebf71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE PARLIAMENTARY COMMITTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Parliamentary Committee is involved in questioning and pressing for details regarding the Commission's actions and decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHRISTIANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GROUP"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Christians are a specific group mentioned as being explicitly excluded from the Commission's microtargeting campaign."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE COMMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commission is the governing body being questioned for its ad campaign and practices, and responsible for various proposals including CSAM-scanning."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JOHANSSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Johansson is a commissioner within the European Commission, being queried about her role and contacts in the ad campaign and CSAM-scanning proposal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MICROSOFT, META, TIKTOK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMPANY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are tech companies contacted by the Commission, indicating potential commercial interests in their products or services."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TWITTER (X)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMPANY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Twitter (also known as X) is another platform contacted by the Commission, similar to Google, Microsoft, and Meta."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLE AND AMAZON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMPANY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Apple and Amazon are also tech companies mentioned as having had contacts with the Commission."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THORN AND BRAVE MOVEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Thorn and Brave Movement are child safety organizations that have been contacted by the Commission."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECH ALLIANCE AND ICANN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tech Alliance and ICANN are also organizations mentioned as having communicated with the Commission."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHRISTIAN EXCLUSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The explicit exclusion of Christians from the Commission’s microtargeting campaign is an event that raises questions about the principles and fairness of the campaign."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXCLUSION CONCERNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Concerns about the exclusion of specific groups, such as Christians, from the microtargeting campaign are a concept being discussed in relation to democratic principles and inclusivity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POLITICAL MICROTARGETING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Political microtargeting refers to the technology used to tailor political messages to specific groups, which is the subject of scrutiny and debate within the European Parliament."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANTI-DEMOCRATIC PRACTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Allegations of anti-democratic practices such as the use of political microtargeting by the Commission and lack of transparency are a concept under examination by MEPs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPIN-DOCTOR TACTICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The use of spin-doctor tactics by the Commission to defend against criticism is a concept highlighted as a potential issue in the relationship between the Commission and journalists."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JOURNALISTIC SCRUTINY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The investigative journalists' report and subsequent scrutiny of the Commission's actions is an event that has prompted a response from the Commission and is being discussed by MEPs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOLIADIS CRITIQUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Foliadis, the journalist involved in the report, is a person who is defending against accusations of spreading disinformation and critiquing the Commission's reaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDIA FREEDOM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Media freedom as a concept is at stake, with concerns that the Commission's tactics may be perceived as a restriction on media freedom if not properly addressed and clarified."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b0966ab70418e77de1708f429152ba62</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commissioner is a European official involved in discussions about content-scanning policies and legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THORN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Thorn is a child safety organization that has been met with by Commissioner twice regarding content-scanning policies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRAVE MOVEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Brave Movement is a child safety organization that has been met with by Commissioner twice regarding content-scanning policies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECH ALLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tech Alliance is an entity that has been met with by Commissioner once regarding content-scanning policies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ICANN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ICANN is an organization that has been met with by Commissioner once regarding content-scanning policies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CSAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CSAM stands for Child Sexual Abuse Material, which is the focus of the content-scanning proposal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EU CENTRE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The EU Centre is an entity likely involved in providing verified indicators of child sexual abuse for the purpose of regulated content-scanning technologies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MASS SURVEILLANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mass Surveillance refers to widespread monitoring of entire populations, typically by government, which Commissioner Johansson refutes as being part of her proposal's approach to content-scanning."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEROGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Derogation in the context refers to legislative exceptions, specifically the temporary ePrivacy derogation that currently allows non-encrypted content scanning for CSAM. Commissioner discusses its replacement by the proposed regulation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREVENTION MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Prevention measures are actions taken by platforms to stop the spread of CSAM and prevent tool abuse, which are required before any detection technology as per Commissioner's proposal.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRATEGIC RESPONSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Strategic Response alludes to the overall stance and activities of European entities in reaction to the unknown intelligence, as highlighted by Commissioner Johansson.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d55a985b6c049d749a46d19de0c5a2af</data>
</node>
