</node>
<node id="&quot;MARINE ORGANISMS&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Great Dying had a catastrophic impact on marine organisms, with a staggering 96% of species going extinct, clearing ecological niches for new life forms to emerge in the following periods.)</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EARLIEST FISH SPECIES&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
  <data key="d1">"Earliest fish species were among the groups that faced extinction during the Great Dying, indicating a major shift in biodiversity and aquatic life.)</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPTILES&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-1070ab0752da87667f6459e567384091</data>
  <data key="d1">"After the Great Dying, reptiles, including early dinosaurs, emerged to fill the ecological niches vacated by the extinct groups, signifying a new phase in the evolutionary timeline.)</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EVOLUTION OF RODENT OF UNUSUAL SIZE&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-a7d1428dd177c265ee0f8475f062a06c</data>
  <data key="d1">"The evolution of the Rodent of Unusual Size was significantly influenced by the presence of Predatory reptiles, which were a driving force for its size reduction."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRIASSIC PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-a7d1428dd177c265ee0f8475f062a06c</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Rodent of Unusual Size reached its maximum size during the Triassic period, a fact tied to a specific time frame in Earth's history."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PODCASTING&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-4858befea8647fc8858e0a35abd02cad</data>
  <data key="d1">"Daniel Ek, as Spotify's CEO, discusses the strategic focus on podcasting and seeks continuous improvements in the business, linking Spotify to the broader podcasting industry trends."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE JOE ROGAN EXPERIENCE, CALL HER DADDY, THIS AMERICAN LIFE&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-4858befea8647fc8858e0a35abd02cad</data>
  <data key="d1">"These podcasts are mentioned as the most-searched, which emphasizes their popularity and influence in the podcasting landscape, potentially impacting Spotify's strategy to tap into such high-demand content."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ISIDRO CONSUNJI&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-79e5ae6ad21314c6c70afb92c3369d42</data>
  <data key="d1">"Isidro Consunji envisions PhilEd as the enabler for Filipino education dreams, suggesting a leadership role in its establishment and funding."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTARY STAMPS&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-172132bcaae33b0503a567b8e442ab73</data>
  <data key="d1">"PhilEd may receive a share of documentary stamp collection taxes, showing a method for additional revenue generation."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOCAL SCHOOL BOARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-172132bcaae33b0503a567b8e442ab73</data>
  <data key="d1">"PhilEd may gain access to Special Education Funds managed by Local School Boards, indicating resource-sharing and collaboration."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AFFECTED BY&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Deep sea creatures rely on dissolved oxygen and are negatively impacted by its reduced availability due to climate change."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AFFECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Climate change is impacting deep sea oxygen levels and the overall health of deep sea ecosystems."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPORTANCE TO DEEP SEA&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Oxygen's role is critical for deep sea creatures, and its decrease due to warming waters poses a significant threat."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOURCE OF OXYGEN FOR DEEP SEA&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Polar regions are the origin of currents that deliver oxygen to deep sea ecosystems, directly influencing their survival."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPPORTS LIFE&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hydrothermal vents provide an environment for life through chemosynthesis, showing alternative energy sources beyond sunlight."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CARRY OXYGEN&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Deep sea currents are responsible for transporting oxygen, a key element for deep sea life, highlighting the connectivity between surface and deep ocean ecosystems."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POTENTIAL DECREASE&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Global oxygen levels in the deep sea are projected to decrease, which could have widespread ecological effects on deep sea life."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNICATOR OF DEEP SEA SCIENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Jon Copley is actively involved in educating the public about deep sea ecosystems, emphasizing the importance of understanding and connection to this often overlooked environment."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPACTS ON&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Climate change mitigation efforts are vital for preventing further decrease in deep sea oxygen levels and protecting the ecosystem."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAUSE OF&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Greenhouse gases, primarily from human activities, are the root cause of global warming and subsequent oxygen depletion in the deep sea."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EFFECTS ON&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ocean warming has multiple effects on deep sea life, including changes in oxygen solubility, metabolic rates, and habitat sustainability."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPACTED BY&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Seawater solubility for oxygen is impacted by temperature, a factor altered by climate change, affecting deep sea organisms' survival."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AT RISK FROM&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Biodiversity in the deep sea is at risk due to changing oxygen levels, temperature, and other factors influenced by climate change."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ROLE IN&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-e52655219f2d13e48ea897fac7c72a41</data>
  <data key="d1">"Environmental scientists play a key role in studying and communicating the impacts of climate change on deep sea ecosystems, advocating for preservation and research."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
