  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ULTRA-PROCESSED FOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ultra-processed foods are categorized by the Yale Food Addiction Scale (YFAS) as having addictive qualities due to their high carbohydrate and fat content."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CANDY, ICE CREAM, AND POTATO CHIPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FOOD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Candy, ice cream, and potato chips are examples of ultra-processed foods mentioned as having addictive properties in the study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUGAR-SWEETENED BEVERAGE TAXES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sugar-sweetened beverage taxes are policy measures taken in some countries to address the consumption of ultra-processed foods, as noted in the study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FDA AND USDA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The FDA (Food and Drug Administration) and USDA (United States Department of Agriculture) are government agencies that could implement food safety regulations, as suggested by the context of the study."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TANYA FREIRICH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tanya Freirich is a registered dietitian nutritionist commenting on the study and the implications of ultra-processed food addiction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOOD CRAVINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Food cravings are discussed as a behavioral response to emotions, stress, and addictive properties of certain foods, as explained by Tanya Freirich."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHRONIC DIETING, FOOD SHAME, FOOD ACCESSIBILITY, EARLY CHILDHOOD FEEDING EXPERIENCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPTS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are factors mentioned as influencing food choices and disordered eating habits, potentially leading to addictive behaviors towards certain foods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUGAR ADDICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sugar addiction is discussed in the context of food choices, with debate on whether sugar can be considered addictive like drugs; the study mentioned does not support sugar addiction as drugs but notes that high sugar intake can lead to craving and consumption patterns similar to addiction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADDICTIVE POTENTIAL OF FOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The concept of the addictive potential of certain foods, particularly ultra-processed foods rich in fats and carbs, is explored, indicating a 'food addiction' similar to substance use disorder."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOPAMINE TOLERANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dopamine tolerance is explained as a phenomenon where increased consumption of addictive foods leads to a diminished pleasure response, potentially contributing to addictive-like eating behaviors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOOD ADDICTION PARALLELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The parallels drawn between the habit-forming nature of sugar-rich foods and drug addiction are discussed, although it is clarified that sugar itself may not cause withdrawal symptoms like true addictive substances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NUTRITION LABELING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The implementation of nutrition labels on ultra-processed foods is mentioned as a measure taken by some countries to inform consumers about the contents and potential addictiveness of these foods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EARLY CHILDHOOD FEEDING EXPERIENCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Early childhood feeding experiences are highlighted as a factor in shaping long-term food choices and potential disordered eating habits, emphasizing the importance of early nutritional education."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHRONIC DIETING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chronic dieting is identified as a factor related to food addiction and disordered eating habits, indicating a cycle that might contribute to the development of such patterns."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOOD SHAME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Food shame is mentioned as a social and psychological factor that can influence food choices and potentially exacerbate disordered eating habits, highlighting the need for a compassionate approach towards eating."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMOTIONAL RESPONSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Emotional responses such as stress and overall metabolic health are acknowledged as factors influencing food choices and cravings, part of a complex interplay leading to addictive-like eating behaviors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRESS AND METABOLIC HEALTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stress and overall metabolic health are noted as contributing factors to food cravings and the propensity for addictive behaviors, emphasizing the multifaceted nature of dietary habits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEARNED FEEDING BEHAVIORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Learned feeding behaviors are discussed as part of the complex web of factors that can lead to food addiction, including habits formed from early experiences and emotional associations with food."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-89039206f849c78fab340ed6f0292d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Foods are linked to the release of dopamine, a feel-good chemical, which can lead to cravings and potentially addictive-like eating behaviors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f98804617aeaf74ea62cbccd7ea7c75</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISORDERED EATING, BINGE-EATING, UNCONTROLLED FOOD CRAVINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These phrases describe specific eating disorders associated with unhealthy food behaviors and the potential for addiction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f98804617aeaf74ea62cbccd7ea7c75</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCESSED FOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Processed Foods are a category of food that typically contains added ingredients like sugar, fats, and preservatives, which are not present in minimally processed foods. These foods are often associated with the discussion on food addiction due to their potential to trigger dopamine release and cravings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f98804617aeaf74ea62cbccd7ea7c75</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINIMALLY PROCESSED FOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minimally Processed Foods refer to foods that have undergone little to no alteration from their natural state and are considered healthier alternatives to processed foods. They are contrasted with processed foods in studies examining food addiction as they may not have the same level of impact on dopamine release and eating cravings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f98804617aeaf74ea62cbccd7ea7c75</data>
</node>
