  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CBD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CBD is mentioned; however, without context, its relevance to the main narrative is unclear. If it pertains specifically to HIV research or CRISPR-based therapies, additional information is required to establish a connection. For now, it's treated as an isolated concept: ""</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLINICAL TRIAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The clinical trial represents a structured scientific investigation to evaluate the safety and efficacy of EBT-101, central to the narrative of advancing HIV treatment potentially through CRISPR technology.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG-TERM FOLLOW-UP STUDY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A long-term follow-up study is planned for trial participants, essential for monitoring long-term outcomes and potential adverse effects after the administration of EBT-101, indicative of the importance of sustained observation in medical research.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YEARS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Years are mentioned in the context of how long it takes for genetic off-target mutations to manifest, which is a cautionary note about the time scale of assessing CRISPR-related complications.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERRUPTIONS TO HIV TREATMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interruptions to HIV treatment are necessary to assess remission potential in cured patients, a process that is controversial due to associated risks and pertinent to understanding the control of HIV infection.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIV REPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HIV replication refers to the process by which HIV spreads and infects more cells, which cART therapies aim to halt. Its control is critical in evaluating the success of potential treatments like EBT-101.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LATENT CELL RESERVOIRS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Latent cell reservoirs are HIV-infected cells that remain inactive but can reignite infection if treatment is paused. Their suppression is a primary goal in HIV treatment research.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMERGING FROM THE SHADOWS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Emerging from the shadows metaphorically describes the potential breakthrough in HIV treatment with EBT-101, suggesting the treatment's impact could bring a new understanding or success against HIV that has been difficult to achieve previously.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REDEFINITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Redefinition implies the possibility of shifting the existing paradigm in HIV treatment, especially if EBT-101 proves its effectiveness and safety in the long term.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL SCIENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
