<node id="&quot;SPATIAL COMPUTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Spatial computing is recognized for its potential to change human-computer interactions, emphasizing the need for technology-informed product design."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRODUCT DESIGN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MISSION/CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Product design is a process that transcends aesthetic choices, focusing on business strategy, user experience, and technology explorations to influence innovation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNOLOGISTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Technologists are described as playing a strategic role in the innovation process, emphasizing the importance of their contribution beyond technical validation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technologists are professionals who add value to the product design process through their expertise on technology characteristics, informing new interaction models and product design."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-997f053f3805e2768d953a251a2dd43c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CUSTOMER-FACING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTEXT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Customer-facing context refers to problems or opportunities directly related to the user's interaction with a product or service."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERNAL-FACING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTEXT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Internal-facing context deals with improving processes and efficiencies within a business or organization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ALICE JOHNSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Alice Johnson is mentioned as a hypothetical example of a technical lead or software developer, which can represent the broader role technologists play in product design and innovation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FRAMING A TECHNOLOGY AS A NATURAL SOLUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Framing technology as a natural solution is a strategy to ensure that technological integration in product design is seamless and addresses real business needs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL TECHNOLOGIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Digital technologies are likened to tangible materials like paint or wood, suggesting that understanding their fundamental nature is essential for product creation and innovation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERT INSIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS/CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Expert insights are valuable contributions that stem from deep technical knowledge, helping shape the trajectory of product design and innovation by translating complex technical details into actionable strategies and concepts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MULTIDISCIPLINARY COLLABORATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Multidisciplinary collaboration emphasizes the importance of diverse perspectives and expertise, which are critical in the product design process for fostering innovation and addressing complex challenges."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOLISTIC PRODUCT EXPERIENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Holistic product experience encompasses all aspects of a user's interaction with a product, from visual design to functionality and usability, suggesting that technology must be integrated in a way that enhances the overall experience."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation process involves a series of steps from ideation to implementation, underscoring the iterative nature of developing successful products and the importance of strategic decision-making throughout this cycle."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRODUCT REACH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Product reach involves expanding the audience or user base for a product, a common goal for product innovation to drive business growth and success.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMBIGUITY IN OUTCOMES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The ambiguity in outcomes of product innovation acknowledges that not all innovations will lead to immediate success, reflecting the trial-and-error nature of the process and the need for patience and resilience.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GAP ANALYSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gap analysis is mentioned as a method to identify areas where a product or business is lacking, a critical step in informing the direction of product innovation and technological application.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESIGN EXPLOITATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Design exploitation refers to the practical use and application of design insights to create viable products and services, highlighting the importance of moving from conceptual design to tangible outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION HYPE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation hype pertains to the often exaggerated expectations and excitement surrounding new technologies, with an emphasis on the need for meaningful, not just superficial, incorporation of technology into products.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VALUE CREATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Value creation is the ultimate goal of product innovation, where successful integration of technology and design leads to products that solve business problems, meet user needs, and contribute to the company's financial success.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNOLOGY ARTICULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Technology articulation is the process of effectively communicating the capabilities and potential impact of a technology within a product context, ensuring that it aligns with business objectives and resonates with stakeholders.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNOLOGY-DRIVEN PRODUCTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Technology-driven products are those shaped significantly by the incorporation of new technologies, showcasing how technology can fundamentally alter product design and user experience.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNOLOGICAL PARTNERSHIPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Technological partnerships refer to collaborations between different stakeholders, such as tech companies and design firms, to leverage combined expertise in product innovation and development.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION LEADERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation leadership involves guiding and inspiring innovation within a company or team, ensuring that strategic insights are at the forefront of the product development process.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNOLOGY LITERACY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Technology literacy is the understanding of technology's role and impact within product design, advocating for a culture where knowledge of technology is shared and used strategically to drive innovation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;USER-CENTRIC APPROACH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A user-centric approach is stressed as a fundamental principle in product design, where the needs and experiences of users guide the incorporation of technology and the strategic direction of innovation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CROSS-FUNCTIONAL TEAM ALIGNMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cross-functional team alignment speaks to the necessity of integrating various departments and expertise within an organization to achieve a cohesive and innovative product design."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COLLABORATIVE INNOVATION ENVIRONMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A collaborative innovation environment is proposed as an ideal setting for product innovation, one that encourages knowledge sharing, joint problem-solving, and the fusion of ideas from various domains.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION CHAMPIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation champions are individuals within an organization who actively promote and drive innovation forward, championing new ideas and spearheading creative solutions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRATEGIC PRODUCT PLANNING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Strategic product planning is described as a methodical process for defining the aims and direction of product development, ensuring that innovation aligns with long-term business objectives and market opportunities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNOLOGY APPLICATION DEPTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The depth of technology application in product innovation refers to the extent to which new technologies are thoughtfully integrated and explored to create meaningful and transformative user experiences.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESIGN-LED INNOVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Design-led innovation is an approach where design principles and insights play a central role in shaping product innovation, influencing the strategic use of technology and business outcomes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION LIFECYCLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The innovation lifecycle is characterized by stages from ideation to market launch, each with its own challenges and considerations for product design and technological integration.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION CULTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation culture signifies an organizational environment that fosters creativity, experimentation, and the willingness to explore new ideas, which is conducive to sustained product innovation and success.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERIENTIAL DESIGN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Experiential design emphasizes creating products that deliver immersive and engaging user experiences, often leveraging technology to enhance the sensory and emotional impact on the user.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGILE INNOVATION METHODOLOGIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Agile innovation methodologies advocate for a flexible and iterative approach to product development, allowing rapid prototyping and adaptation based on user feedback and changing market conditions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION STRATEGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation strategy outlines the overarching plan for how a company approaches product innovation, including goals, priorities, and tactics to navigate technology trends and business opportunities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION PORTFOLIO MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation portfolio management involves curating a mix of products and projects that balance risk and reward, ensuring sustained innovation and growth for the organization.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION AUDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An innovation audit assesses how well an organization is managing its innovation activities, identifying strengths and areas for improvement to optimize product design and innovation outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION IMPACT ASSESSMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation impact assessment measures the effect of product innovation on business performance, user satisfaction, and market position, serving as a feedback loop for continuous improvement.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION BENCHMARKING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation benchmarking involves comparing a company's innovation practices and outcomes against industry standards or competitors, providing insights into areas of competitive advantage or needed improvement.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSTAINABILITY IN INNOVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sustainability in innovation stresses the importance of considering long-term environmental and social impacts when developing new products and technologies to ensure responsible and ethical growth."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION RESILIENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation resilience refers to an organization's ability to sustain product innovation and adapt to challenges over time, ensuring continuous evolution and relevance in changing markets.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION COMPETENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation competence captures the collective skills and knowledge within an organization that drive successful product innovation, including technical expertise, creative thinking, and strategic acumen.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION CAPACITY BUILDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation capacity building involves actions to develop and enhance an organization's ability to innovate, including training, hiring, and fostering a culture of learning and experimentation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION CULTURE INFLUENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The influence of innovation culture pertains to how the prevailing attitudes, behaviors, and practices within an organization support or hinder product innovation, impacting its success."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION METRICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation metrics are tools used to quantify and assess various aspects of innovation, such as the rate of idea generation, time to market, and return on investment, to guide strategic product development decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION TREND ANALYSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation trend analysis examines emerging trends and technologies to inform product innovation strategies and stay ahead of the competitive curve."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION LEARNING CURVES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation learning curves describe the stages of learning and adoption of new ideas and technologies within a product innovation process, from initial concept to market adoption and beyond."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION ADAPTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation adaptation refers to the ability of a product or business to adjust and evolve in response to changing market conditions, user needs, and technological advancements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION AGILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation agility represents the ability to quickly pivot or adapt in product innovation efforts, enabling responsiveness to new challenges and opportunities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION RESILIENCE FRAMEWORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An innovation resilience framework provides guidelines and best practices for building and sustaining resilience in product innovation, enabling companies to withstand and thrive amidst change and uncertainty."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION NETWORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation networks consist of relationships and partnerships between individuals, organizations, and resources, which collectively contribute to a rich ecosystem of ideas, collaborations, and support for ongoing innovation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION ECOSYSTEM SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation ecosystem services are the support systems, resources, and infrastructure that facilitate product innovation, such as market research, technology sharing, and collaborative platforms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION GOVERNANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation governance refers to the rules, policies, and oversight that guide innovation activities within an organization, ensuring alignment with business objectives and strategic priorities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION STRATEGY ALIGNMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation strategy alignment ensures that product innovation activities are in sync with the overall strategic vision and goals of an organization, optimizing resource allocation and shaping innovation initiatives that deliver value and competitive advantage.&lt;SEP&gt;"Innovation strategy alignment ensures that product innovation efforts are in sync with the overall strategic vision and goals of an organization, maximizing the impact of investments and efforts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION EFFICIENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation efficiency focuses on maximizing the effectiveness and productivity of product innovation processes while minimizing waste and redundancy, optimizing resource utilization and speeding up development.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION RISK MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation risk management entails identifying, assessing, and mitigating the risks associated with product innovation, allowing for informed decision-making and strategic planning."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION FORESIGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation foresight involves anticipating future trends, disruptions, and emerging opportunities, enabling proactive strategic planning and decision-making in product innovation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION FORESIGHTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation foresighting uses insights, forecasts, and scenario planning to anticipate future developments in technology and the market, informing the strategic direction of product innovation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION SUSTAINABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation sustainability emphasizes the need to consider long-term environmental, social, and ethical implications when developing new products and technologies, promoting responsible and ethical innovation practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION ATTRIBUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation attribution refers to the recognition and acknowledgment of contributions and intellectual property within the product innovation process, ensuring fairness and transparency in the attribution of ideas and advancements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION ACCOUNTABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation accountability involves the responsibilities and obligations tied to product innovation, including ethical considerations, resource management, and performance outcomes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION TRANSPARENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation transparency is the openness and clarity in sharing information and progress related to product innovation efforts, fostering trust and collaboration among stakeholders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION FEEDBACK LOOPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation feedback loops are mechanisms for collecting, analyzing, and incorporating feedback on product innovation, creating a continuous cycle of improvement and adaptation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION STRATEGY REALIGNMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation strategy realignment is the process of adjusting and refining an organization's innovation strategy to align with changing business environments and emerging technologies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INNOVATION OPPORTUNITY IDENTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Innovation opportunity identification is the process of scanning the market and identifying unmet needs or areas for growth that can be addressed through product innovation, driving strategic decision-making and prioritization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e2f2555285deec6246e71979792ba10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESIGNERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Designers utilize information provided by technologists to shape and exploit technologies in visual and interaction design, acting as intermediaries between design and technology."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-997f053f3805e2768d953a251a2dd43c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRODUCT STRATEGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Product Strategy refers to the comprehensive planning and decision-making process regarding the development and growth of a product, which benefits from the inclusion of technologists."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-997f053f3805e2768d953a251a2dd43c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRODUCT DESIGN PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Product Design Process is enriched by the involvement of technologists who provide a technology perspective, leading to innovation in the design and implementation of products."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-997f053f3805e2768d953a251a2dd43c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRODUCT ECOSYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Product Ecosystem represents the network of products, technologies, and strategies that interact and influence each other, requiring a deep understanding of the technology ontology and phenomenology."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-997f053f3805e2768d953a251a2dd43c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PEDANTIC NATURE OF TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Pedantic Nature of Technology refers to the detailed and intricate aspects of technology that must be understood to integrate and innovate effectively within product design."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-997f053f3805e2768d953a251a2dd43c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRODUCT GROWTH STAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Product Growth Stage refers to the phase in a product's lifecycle where it is expanding in size, reach, or complexity, necessitating a deeper understanding of technology and strategic planning."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-997f053f3805e2768d953a251a2dd43c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STABLE PRODUCT STAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stable Product Stage is the phase where a product maintains a consistent presence in the market, requiring ongoing optimization and understanding of existing technologies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-997f053f3805e2768d953a251a2dd43c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL TOOLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
