  <data key="d2">chunk-997f053f3805e2768d953a251a2dd43c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CROSS-FUNCTIONAL TEAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cross-functional Teams are groups consisting of members from various departments working together towards a common project, such as integrating technology in product design, fostering innovation and collaboration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-997f053f3805e2768d953a251a2dd43c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PASTOR JESSE BRADLEY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pastor Jesse Bradley is a minister at Grace Community Church who addresses faith dilemmas and the concept of positive thinking to improve mental health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pastor Jesse Bradley is a religious leader addressing the decline of faith in America and the importance of trust in God for the nation's future."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e68b77424fb2b72802b14e0ec8061db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a39abd8a9eeb3b15da9c5598baf849a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRACE COMMUNITY CHURCH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Grace Community Church is the place where Pastor Jesse Bradley ministers to people and shares insights on positive thinking."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grace Community Church is the specific religious organization Pastor Jesse Bradley is affiliated with, indicating its role in the context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e68b77424fb2b72802b14e0ec8061db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a39abd8a9eeb3b15da9c5598baf849a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IN GOD WE TRUST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"In God We Trust is a national motto and symbol of American faith, which Pastor Bradley notes appears to be waning in its influence and importance."&lt;SEP&gt;"In God We Trust is mentioned as a concept on currency and its constitutional status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e68b77424fb2b72802b14e0ec8061db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e81e82925522df3b923fcbf21587c3cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAITH IN AMERICA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Faith in America refers to the spiritual belief and religious practices that are prevalent within the United States, noting a decline according to Pastor Jesse Bradley."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e68b77424fb2b72802b14e0ec8061db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CULTURAL UPHEAVAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cultural upheaval describes the significant changes and shifts in societal values, which Pastor Bradley associates with the waning of religious faith, including a decrease in attendance at religious services and Sunday worship."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e68b77424fb2b72802b14e0ec8061db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL DECODY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Social decay denotes the breakdown of structures and traditions that have historically been supported by a collective religious faith, including family units and educational systems, as noted by Pastor Jesse Bradley."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e68b77424fb2b72802b14e0ec8061db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELIGIOUS FAITHLESSNESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Religious faithlessness indicates a trend in the United States toward secularism and the diminishing number of individuals identifying with a particular faith, as reflected in both survey results and anecdotal evidence mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e68b77424fb2b72802b14e0ec8061db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENTERTAINMENT, TECHNOLOGY, GOVERNMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"IDOLS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Entertainment, technology, and government have been identified by Pastor Jesse Bradley as modern distractions or false idols that have supplanted the central role of faith in people's lives."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e68b77424fb2b72802b14e0ec8061db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELIGIONAL FREEDOM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Religious freedom is a foundational value in the United States, rooted in the nation's founding and enshrined in documents like the Declaration of Independence and the Constitution, emphasizing the non-denominational nature of the Creator and the right to choose one's faith without coercion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e68b77424fb2b72802b14e0ec8061db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BENEATH THE SURVEYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SURVEY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Surveys are mentioned as a body of evidence that reflects the trends in declining religious engagement and increasing secularism among Americans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e68b77424fb2b72802b14e0ec8061db</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BROTHER IN MISSOURI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The reunion of siblings with their 3-year-old brother in Michigan after his hospital stay for cancer treatment illustrates a personal element that contrasts with the broader theme of spiritual decline discussed by Pastor Jesse Bradley, emphasizing family and healing in a faith-based context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e68b77424fb2b72802b14e0ec8061db</data>
</node>
