<node id="&quot;MONETARY POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Monetary Policy involves the management of a country's money supply and interest rates by a central bank to influence economic conditions, including inflation, employment, and economic growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monetary Policy refers to the actions of a central bank or other regulatory body that determine the size and rate of growth of the money supply in an economy, which in turn affects the economy's interest rates, inflation, and economic growth."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8a16bacbe3e61a320a283eaf350790f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3f4e147d3daddec3b2e694fb2becca7</data>
