  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rebuilding a jet mid-flight refers to the challenge of rapidly restructuring the team while Steph Curry is still active and the trade deadline approaches.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de400612098396a745c0a6e77fc1df10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YOUNGER TEAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Younger Team implies a team that could potentially acquire draft picks like Kuminga or Moody, which would be an investment in the future as the current team faces age-related challenges.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de400612098396a745c0a6e77fc1df10</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BASIC AI MODELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Basic AI models are referred to as foundation models, which are a type of general purpose AI models that can be used for various tasks and integrated into different systems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOUNDATION MODELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Foundation models are a subset of general purpose AI models that underpin systems like ChatGPT, capable of being adapted for a wide range of applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AI ACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"AI Act refers to the legal framework agreed upon in the EU for regulating AI, ensuring compliance with safety, innovation, and fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;"The AI Act is the proposed comprehensive legal framework for regulating artificial intelligence, being developed and agreed upon by EU lawmakers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The AI Act represents the agreed political deal on regulating artificial intelligence in the EU and is considered a historic milestone.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH RISK THRESHOLD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The high risk threshold is a benchmark set for classifying AI models as having significant impact, measured in floating point operations (FLOPs)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLOPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"FLOPs (floating point operations per second) measure the computational power required for AI model training, used to assess the risk level of AI systems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AI OFFICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"AI Office is an expert body designated to set risk classification thresholds for GPAIs and contribute to the oversight of AI technologies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The AI Office is a new expert oversight body to be established within the Commission for developing benchmarks to assess AI models, indicating its role in the ongoing regulation refinement process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The AI Office is a proposed entity within the EU's executive to coordinate AI regulation enforcement and oversee advanced AI models, established as part of the agreement's implementation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1165227899625387967696e9c99c63bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b86098cf9342b7ec411c2cd37c240ff1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPUTE USED TO TRAIN MODELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The computational resource expenditure during the training of AI models is a factor in determining their risk classification under the AI Act."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WATERMARKING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Watermarking refers to the process of embedding information into content to verify its authenticity or origin, which in this context is applied to generative AI outputs for transparency and traceability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODEL RISK ASSESSMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Model Risk Assessment is the process by which AI models are evaluated for potential risks they may pose, highlighting a crucial aspect of AI governance and compliance within the new legal framework.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SYSTEMIC RISK MITIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Systemic Risk Mitigation refers to the proactive testing and measures taken to reduce the risks associated with AI models, a critical concern addressed by the AI Act for high-risk AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EX ANTE REGULATORY REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ex Ante Regulatory Requirements are proactive legal and compliance measures that companies must take before deploying AI models, reflecting the preventative nature of the AI Act's approach to AI risk management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERT OVERSIGHT BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Expert Oversight Body, or AI Office, is a new entity within the EU Commission tasked with setting benchmarks for AI model assessment, demonstrating the institutional response to AI regulation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE GOVERNANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Artificial Intelligence Governance refers to the principles and regulations that guide the ethical, safe, and fair use and development of AI, integral to the EU's efforts in AI regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGISLATIVE PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Legislative Process denotes the sequence of steps taken by lawmakers to develop and agree upon laws, specifically referencing the voting and discussions involved in the AI Act's creation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATORY THRESHOLD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulatory Threshold refers to the criteria used to classify AI models based on their potential risks, such as compute usage (FLOPs), which are subject to change according to technological advancements and oversight decisions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHATGPT AND GEMINI MODELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ChatGPT and Gemini Models are specific instances of AI models that could be impacted by the regulatory framework, offering concrete examples of the types of technologies being discussed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a04636b49c5d8346d1ca2fd6e5201fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSION OFFICIAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commission official represents an individual involved in the decision-making process, discussing regulatory details for AI technologies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b86098cf9342b7ec411c2cd37c240ff1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GPAI MODEL MAKERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"GPAI model makers are entities responsible for creating Generative Pre-Trained Algorithms and are subject to regulatory obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b86098cf9342b7ec411c2cd37c240ff1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EU COPYRIGHT DIRECTIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"EU Copyright Directive is a legislative framework that governs copyright rules and regulations within the EU, relevant to GPAI compliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b86098cf9342b7ec411c2cd37c240ff1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATIONAL EXPERTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"National experts are individuals recruited to assist the AI Office with AI-related matters in Member States."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b86098cf9342b7ec411c2cd37c240ff1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCIENTIFIC ADVISORY PANEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Scientific advisory panel is a body that will aid the AI Office by understanding AI capabilities and identifying new risks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b86098cf9342b7ec411c2cd37c240ff1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GENERATIVE PRE-TRAINED ALGORITHMS (GPAIS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"GPAIs are AI technologies that are under regulatory scrutiny and must comply with the AI Act's guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b86098cf9342b7ec411c2cd37c240ff1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WATERMARKING TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Watermarking technology is the state-of-the-art technology used to mark AI-produced text, crucial for identifying the source of generated content and ensuring compliance with regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b86098cf9342b7ec411c2cd37c240ff1</data>
</node>
