</node>
<node id="&quot;CINERAMA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cinerama is an older 35mm projector technology used in the 1950s to project a single image onto a deeply curved screen, a precursor to modern 360-degree cinema technologies like the Sphere."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIRCLE-VISION 360&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Circle-Vision 360 is a 1950s technology with nine cameras positioned in a circle to create 360-degree film images, used as a historical reference point for the Sphere's capabilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
