<node id="&quot;ARTIFICIAL WIND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Artificial wind is one of the haptic elements used in the Sphere venue to simulate environmental effects during performances or presentations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Scents are among the haptic features of the Sphere venue, providing olfactory stimulation that corresponds with different scenes or moments.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KEY MOMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Key moments are specific instances during a performance where haptic feedback like wind and scents are intensified to enhance the storytelling experience.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FILMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Films are part of the content offered in the Sphere venue, demonstrating the venue's capacity to host high-resolution, immersive cinematic experiences.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;360-DEGREE SCREENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"360-degree screens refer to the Sphere's capacity to present content in a full 360-degree format, which is a pivotal aspect of its immersive technology.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DARREN ARONOFSKY”">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Darren Aronofsky is an acclaimed filmmaker who had an event at the Sphere, showcasing the venue's versatility for premiering high-quality productions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POSTCARD FROM EARTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Postcard From Earth is a film that premiered at the Sphere, exemplifying the venue's capability to host immersive and high-quality visual storytelling.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUZIE MILLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Suzie Miller is an Australian playwright who has adapted her work for performance at various venues, including the Sphere, showcasing the venue's adaptability for diverse forms of storytelling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HAROLD PINTER THEATRE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Harold Pinter Theatre is a London theater where Suzie Miller's play, Prima Facie, has been performed, indicating the range of venues the Sphere compares with in size and experience.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JOHN GOLDEN THEATRE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"John Golden Theatre is a Broadway theatre where Suzie Miller's play has been staged, offering another point of comparison in terms of scale and audience experience to the Sphere venue.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e063d80990d5bf2a66b1e8280adade80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HELMHOLTZ INSTITUTE FOR RNA-BASED INFECTION RESEARCH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Helmholtz Institute for RNA-based Infection Research is a research group in Germany focusing on RNA synthetic biology related to infections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAUL TURNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paul Turner is the director of the Center for Phage Biology and Therapy at Yale University, an expert in phage therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paul Turner is the director of the Center for Phage Biology and Therapy at Yale University, contributing to the discussion on phage therapy and antibiotic resistance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BACTERIOPHAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bacteriophages, or bacteria-infecting viruses, are proposed alternatives to antibiotics that infect and kill bacteria."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;E. COLI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"E. coli is a type of bacterium that can be affected by bacteriophages like U136B, used to slow down its resistance to drugs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESISTANCE GENES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Resistance genes are genetic elements that can be shared among bacteria, leading to the spread of drug resistance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CENTERS FOR DISEASE CONTROL AND PREVENTION (CDC)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CDC is an agency focused on public health, tracking bacterial resistance among other threats."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION (WHO)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"WHO is an international body that defines and monitors drug-resistant bacteria of global concern."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BROAD-SPECTRUM ANTIBIOTICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Broad-spectrum antibiotics are drugs that target both major classes of bacteria, but their widespread use contributes to the development of resistance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DRUG-RESISTANT BACTERIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Drug-resistant bacteria are bacteria that have developed resistance to antibiotics and are a global health threat."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Antibiotics are drugs used to kill or slow the growth of bacteria, but their overuse and misuse are leading to increased resistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are referenced in relation to treating bacterial infections, though the specific pathogen's resistance is not yet determined, highlighting the medical challenge in treating the illness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09d7ee9151d3af457229ac9e971a0d89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GLOBAL SCALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Global scale refers to a worldwide perspective or actions taken across the world, in this context relating to the usage and resistance to antibiotics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTIC-RESISTANT INFECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Antibiotic-resistant infections refer to bacterial infections that are not responsive to standard antibiotic treatments, posing a significant challenge to global health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRAM-POSITIVE BACTERIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gram-positive bacteria are one class of bacteria that antibiotics target, distinguishing them by their cell wall structure and are affected by antibiotic resistance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRAM-NEGATIVE BACTERIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gram-negative bacteria are another class of bacteria targeted by antibiotics, characterized by a thinner cell wall and also impacted by antibiotic resistance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOSPITALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hospitals are common settings where antibiotic-resistant bacteria are often encountered due to the high use of antibiotics and surgical interventions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SURGICAL INSTRUMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Surgical instruments are tools that can potentially spread antibiotic-resistant bacteria if not properly sterilized, playing a role in the transmission of such infections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9959472053a8605959e9369f5069274</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YALE UNIVERSITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Yale University is the institution affiliated with Paul Turner, involved in phage therapy research and exploring alternatives to antibiotics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PHAGE THERAPY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Phage therapy is a topic of discussion for its potential to combat antibiotic resistance and its targeted approach to bacterial infections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTIC RESISTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Antibiotic resistance is a significant challenge in treating bacterial infections, where pathogens evolve mechanisms to survive drug exposure, necessitating the development of new treatment strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic resistance is highlighted as a major issue that phage therapy could potentially overcome compared to traditional antibiotics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRISPR-CAS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CRISPR-Cas is mentioned as a gene-editing tool originally derived from bacterial immune systems and its use in targeting specific DNA sequences within bacteria."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESIGNER MOLECULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Designer molecules, specifically peptide nucleic acids, are introduced as a new approach to target and kill specific bacteria without the broad-spectrum effects of traditional antibiotics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPASSIONATE USE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compassionate Use refers to a regulatory framework where treatments are provided outside of standard clinical trials, often when patients have no other options."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;100 PATIENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A study involving 100 patients receiving phages alongside antibiotics demonstrates the real-world application and observation of phage therapy's efficacy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LUNG AND FOOT INFECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SPECIFIC LOCATIONS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lung and foot infections are mentioned as the types of infections where phage therapy might show effectiveness in certain trials."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;800-PERSON TRIAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A midstage clinical trial with approximately 800 participants testing CRISPR-enhanced phage therapy, indicating the scale of trials for potential new treatments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOCUS BIOSCIENCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Locus Biosciences is a biotech company testing CRISPR-enhanced phage therapy, showcasing the commercial and clinical development stage of new treatments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHASE BEISEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chase Beisel is a co-founder and scientific adviser for Locus Biosciences, contributing to the development and testing of CRISPR-enhanced phage therapies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEQUENCE-SPECIFIC TARGETING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sequence-specific targeting is emphasized as a key advantage of CRISPR-Cas technology, allowing precise interaction with bacterial DNA without affecting other bacteria."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SNIPPING DNA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The act of snipping DNA is a function of the Cas enzyme within the CRISPR-Cas system, representing a key mechanism in gene editing and bacterial targeting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RNA STRAND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The RNA strand is part of the CRISPR-Cas system, guiding the Cas enzyme to the correct location on the DNA to make the cut, crucial for precision in gene editing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LETHAL AUTOIMMUNE REACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A lethal autoimmune reaction can occur if CRISPR-Cas mistakenly targets bacterial DNA, leading to exploration of safety measures in treatment development."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAB-MADE MOLECULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lab-made molecules, such as peptide nucleic acids, are represented as innovative alternatives to antibiotics, focusing on precision and reduced resistance development."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEALTHY BACTERIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Healthy bacteria are considered in the context of phage therapy to ensure that beneficial bacterial populations are not harmed, which is important for maintaining microbiome balance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BACTERIAL CELLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bacterial cells are the primary targets for the new bacteria-killing approaches discussed, with considerations for their preservation to maintain health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BACTERIAL SURVIVAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bacterial survival is a focus when discussing the effectiveness of novel treatments, where the goal is to eliminate pathogens without allowing the development of resistance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-810de5a13faa41c026bb6e71be802f22</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PEPTIDES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Peptides are engineered molecules being researched as a new approach to target bacteria, specifically by blocking essential protein synthesis without harming human cells."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PNAS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PNAs (Peptide Nucleic Acids) are a type of engineered molecule designed to interfere with bacterial protein synthesis by binding to mRNA, without being able to enter bacterial cells themselves and requiring attachment to other molecules that can penetrate the bacterial cell wall."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BACTERIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANISM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bacteria are the target of the engineered molecules being discussed, which aim to inhibit their protein production essential for survival."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MRNA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"mRNA (messenger RNA) is the genetic molecule that carries instructions for protein construction from the cell's nucleus to its protein synthesis sites, and is targeted by PNAs and other engineered molecules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EFFLUX PUMPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Efflux pumps are bacterial mechanisms that contribute to antibiotic resistance by expelling antibiotics from the bacterial cell, a concept relevant to the discussion of targeting proteins that contribute to such resistance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LYSINS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lysins are enzymes used in nature by phages to kill bacteria by cutting through their cell walls, a method that is less likely to lead to resistance due to the essential nature of cell-wall components targeted by lysins."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PHAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Phages are viruses that infect bacteria, using lysins to kill them, and are mentioned in the context of natural antibacterial mechanisms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTIC STEWARDSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Antibiotic Stewardship refers to the responsible management of antibiotic use to prevent the rise of antibiotic resistance and improve patient outcomes, as discussed by Dr. Shruti Gohil."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENGINEERED MOLECULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Engineered molecules encompass the various technologies and substances, such as PNAs and lysins, that are being developed to target and combat bacterial resistance in innovative ways."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TARGETING ANTIBIOTIC RESISTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Targeting antibiotic resistance is a key strategy in the development of new antibacterial treatments, focusing on mechanisms like efflux pumps and disabling enzymes that contribute to bacterial survival against antibiotics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MESSENGER RNA (MRNA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL ELEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"messenger RNA is a crucial component in the process of protein synthesis, which is targeted by new antibacterial technologies like PNAs to disrupt bacterial growth."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ESSENTIAL CELL-WALL COMPONENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL ELEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Essential cell-wall components are targets for lysins, highlighting their importance in bacterial cell integrity and as a point of vulnerability in antibacterial strategies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NARROW-SPECTRUM DRUGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Narrow-spectrum drugs are antibiotics that target specific types of bacteria, which could reduce the development of resistance compared to broad-spectrum antibiotics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8933a9e1b02edb37aaa2906c3ed684b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESPIRATORY ILLNESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Respiratory Illness is the central event being discussed, affecting a variety of dog breeds and causing symptoms like cough and pneumonia."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09d7ee9151d3af457229ac9e971a0d89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEW HAMPSHIRE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"New Hampshire is one of the states where cases of the respiratory illness in dogs have been reported, indicating a geographical relevance to the investigation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09d7ee9151d3af457229ac9e971a0d89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF NEW HAMPSHIRE’S VETERINARY DIAGNOSIS LABORATORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"University of New Hampshire’s Veterinary Diagnosis Laboratory is one of the research institutions involved in identifying the pathogen causing the respiratory illness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09d7ee9151d3af457229ac9e971a0d89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUBBARD CENTER FOR GENOME STUDIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hubbard Center for Genome Studies is another research institution collaborating in the investigation of the respiratory illness in dogs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09d7ee9151d3af457229ac9e971a0d89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DR. DAVID NEEDLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dr. David Needle is a pathology section chief at the University of New Hampshire, contributing to the research on the pathogen."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09d7ee9151d3af457229ac9e971a0d89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAWRENCE GORDON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lawrence Gordon is a graduate student at the University of New Hampshire who conducted significant work in identifying genetic material from the pathogen in samples."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09d7ee9151d3af457229ac9e971a0d89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;USDA ANIMAL AND PLANT HEALTH INSPECTION SERVICE (APHIS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"USDA Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service (APHIS) is involved in collaborating with state animal health officials and diagnostic labs concerning the respiratory illness in dogs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09d7ee9151d3af457229ac9e971a0d89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MIKE STEPIEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mike Stepien, a spokesperson for APHIS, communicates updates on the respiratory illness in dogs to the public and media."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09d7ee9151d3af457229ac9e971a0d89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DR. KARL E. JANDREY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dr. Karl E. Jandrey is a professor providing expertise on respiratory infections in dogs and potential case reports from other states."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09d7ee9151d3af457229ac9e971a0d89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COLIN PARRISH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Colin Parrish is a professor of virology who comments on the likelihood that the cause of illness will be bacterial rather than viral.&lt;SEP&gt;"Colin Parrish is a veterinary expert providing insights into the likelihood of a viral cause for illness in dogs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09d7ee9151d3af457229ac9e971a0d89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e0a748f39bd8012e95274edcd8be20</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OREGON AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT&quot;">
