  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Horror Recommendation List is a compilation of horror films and series curated to showcase intellectually and viscerally stimulating horror films, presumably intended for sharing with others who enjoy the genre."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-508b703dace19f04ad098710b945b2ee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CROWDSOURCED INSIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Crowdsourced Insights refers to the process of gathering suggestions and opinions from a broad group of people, in this case, for horror movie recommendations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-508b703dace19f04ad098710b945b2ee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NETFLIX UNAVAILABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Netflix Unavailability signifies the circumstance when certain movies like Sputnik were not available on Netflix, impacting viewers' ability to watch them instantly on the platform."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-508b703dace19f04ad098710b945b2ee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VIDEO-ON-DEMAND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Video-on-Demand technology allows users to watch films at their convenience, a service that had the impact on the availability of Sputnik after its Tribeca Film Festival world premiere."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-508b703dace19f04ad098710b945b2ee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SKYPE PHENOMENON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Skype Phenomenon refers to the increasing relevance and impact of video calls, particularly in the context of horror experiences as depicted in Unfriended and its sequel."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-508b703dace19f04ad098710b945b2ee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DARK WEB HORROR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dark Web Horror represents the horror narrative extension into the digital realm, as seen in the sequel to Unfriended, Unfriended: Dark Web."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-508b703dace19f04ad098710b945b2ee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERNATURAL ELEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Supernatural Elements are integral to many horror movies, including the series Unfriended and The Thing, where unknown, eerie forces play a significant role."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-508b703dace19f04ad098710b945b2ee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARANOIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paranoia is a recurring theme in horror narratives, particularly in The Thing and Unfriended, contributing to the tension and fear experienced by the characters and audiences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-508b703dace19f04ad098710b945b2ee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTELLECTUAL STIMULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intellectual Stimulation denotes the stimulating narratives and creative elements in horror films and series that challenge viewers' perceptions and provoke deep thought, as emphasized in the list and the descriptions of the movies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-508b703dace19f04ad098710b945b2ee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LUPITA NYONG’O&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lupita Nyong’o stars in Us, performing in a brief but impactful role as a family friend."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-94eb56a05dcca2101eca2973d4425bbf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOPPELGÄNGERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Doppelgängers are entities that mirror the family members, driving the central conflict in the movie Us as they commit violent acts against the Wilsons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-94eb56a05dcca2101eca2973d4425bbf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COUNCIL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Council is part of the bloc’s co-legislators that, along with the European Parliament, are involved in the AI regulatory process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;URSULA VON DER LEYEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ursula von der Leyen is the President of the European Union who prioritized trustworthy AI development during her term.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROHIBITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Prohibitions are specific restrictions placed on the use of certain AI technologies to protect fundamental rights and safety.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BIOMETRIC CATEGORISATION SYSTEMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Biometric categorisation systems are AI technologies prohibited due to their potential misuse of sensitive characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNTARGETED SCRAPING OF FACIAL IMAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Untargeted scraping of facial images is prohibited to prevent the creation of facial recognition databases without consent.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMOTION RECOGNITION IN THE WORKPLACE AND EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The use of AI for emotion recognition in education and workplace environments is prohibited to protect privacy and individual rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL SCORING BASED ON SOCIAL BEHAVIOUR OR PERSONAL CHARACTERISTICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"AI systems that score individuals based on social or personal characteristics are prohibited to prevent discrimination and protect privacy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AI SYSTEMS THAT MANIPULATE HUMAN BEHAVIOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"AI systems designed to manipulate human behavior are prohibited to protect free will and autonomy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AI USED TO EXPLOIT VULNERABILITIES OF PEOPLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"AI technologies that exploit people's vulnerabilities are prohibited to protect their rights and safety."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REMOTE BIOMETRIC IDENTIFICATION TECHNOLOGY IN PUBLIC PLACES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Remote biometric identification technology used by law enforcement in public places is subject to narrow exceptions and safeguards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REAL-TIME PUBLIC FACIAL RECOGNITION (RBI)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Real-time public facial recognition is one of the technologies that member states resisted a full ban on, despite opposition from the Parliament.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH RISK AIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"High risk AIs are AI systems that pose significant potential harm and are subject to strict regulatory requirements.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOUNDATIONAL MODELS/GENERAL PURPOSE AIS (GPAIS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Foundational models/GPAIs are types of AI systems that are foundational to generative AI applications, highlighting their importance and the discussion around their regulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Foundational models/general purpose AIs are a category of AI systems that are subject to a two-tier system of guardrails, with transparency requirements for lower-tier AIs.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNDAMENTAL RIGHTS IMPACT ASSESSMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fundamental rights impact assessments are requirements for AI systems that evaluate the potential effects on fundamental rights.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSURANCE AND BANKING SECTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Insurance and banking sectors are areas where AI systems impacting fundamental rights are subject to assessments and regulations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLAINTS ABOUT AI SYSTEMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The right for citizens to lodge complaints about AI systems is established in the AI Act, ensuring accountability and recourse for affected individuals.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUMAN RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Human rights refer to the basic rights and freedoms that individuals are entitled to, which are protected under the AI Act from potential AI-related abuses.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL RIGHTS GROUP EDRI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Digital rights group EDRi is a member of civil society groups that have reacted skeptically to the AI Act, expressing concerns that the limitations on state agencies' use of biometric identification technologies may not be sufficient to fully safeguard human rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIVIL SOCIETY GROUPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Civil society groups represent a collective of organizations and individuals advocating for the protection of human rights, who in this context are reacting to the AI Act's limitations on biometric technologies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df1e54144826fa9e7de615586ba59989</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EU COPYRIGHT LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"EU copyright law refers to the legal framework governing copyright within the European Union, which now includes technical documentation requirements for AI systems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CO-LEGISLATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Co-legislators are individuals involved in the legislative process, responsible for working together to draft, amend, and approve laws in the EU."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CARME ARTIGAS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Carme Artigas is Spain's secretary of state for digital and AI issues, leading the Council's negotiations for the agreement, indicating her prominent role in the matter.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COUNCIL'S NEGOTIATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Council's negotiations refer to the discussions and deliberations conducted by the Council of the European Union on the AI regulation package."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL CERTAINTY WITH TECHNICAL CERTAINTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal certainty with technical certainty refers to the regulatory goal of creating clear, enforceable, and predictable rules for AI that also align with the technical capabilities and innovations in the field.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DRAGOȘ TUDORACHE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dragoș Tudorache is a co-rapporteur for the EU Parliament, involved in shaping and endorsing the AI legislation with consideration for human rights and European values.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRANDO BENIFEI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Brando Benifei is also a co-rapporteur for the EU Parliament, emphasizing the protection of fundamental rights in AI development and the achievement of significant milestones in AI regulation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HORIZONTAL LEGISLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Horizontal legislation describes laws that apply across various sectors or activities, in this case, AI development, across the continent of Europe, indicating a comprehensive approach to regulation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EUROPEAN DEVELOPERS, STARTUPS, AND SCALE-UPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GROUP"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This group consists of European entities involved in AI development, supported by the legislation through legal and technical certainty to foster innovation and growth.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREDICTIVE POLICING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"USE CASE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Predictive Policing is a specific application of AI for law enforcement that is banned under the new AI Act, signifying its controversial and regulated status within the legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BIOMETRIC CATEGORIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"USE CASE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Biometric Categorization involves the use of AI to categorize individuals based on biological or physical characteristics, which is also prohibited under the AI Act, emphasizing the act's stance on privacy and individual rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SYSTEMIC RISK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Systemic Risk refers to the potential for AI systems to cause widespread or significant adverse effects on individuals or society, necessitating assessment and mitigation as part of the AI Act's regulatory framework.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODEL EVALUATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REQUIREMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Model Evaluations are part of the compliance process for high-impact GPAIs, requiring them to be assessed and mitigated as per the AI Act's regulations to ensure safety and reliability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADVERSARIAL TESTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REQUIREMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adversarial Testing involves challenging AI systems to ensure they can cope with unexpected or malicious inputs, a mandatory aspect of AI Act compliance for high-risk AI models.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERIOUS INCIDENTS REPORTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REQUIREMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Serious Incidents Reporting is a requirement for AI systems to report significant malfunctions or failures, ensuring transparency and accountability in the AI Act's framework.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GLOBAL CONVERGENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GOAL"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Global Convergence is the aim to align AI standards and regulations internationally, as highlighted by the co-rapporteurs, to address the global challenges and ethical implications of AI technologies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAFEGUARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Safeguards are measures put in place within the AI Act to protect fundamental rights and ensure trust in AI systems, which are crucial for the responsible development of AI.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISIONAL AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL INSTRUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Provisional Agreement refers to the temporary arrangement made by the EU Council regarding the phased implementation of the AI Act, giving industries time to adapt to new regulations while maintaining control over compliance for smaller entities.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMES AND START-UPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AFFECTED GROUPS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"SMEs and start-ups are specifically considered in the legislation, with potential for smaller fines under the provisional agreement, recognizing the importance of nurturing innovation in these segments.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4e0451e53ccec6fb06b6b911fe40f3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JEAN-NOËL BARROT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Jean-Noël Barrot is France's digital minister, involved in analyzing and responding to the AI rules agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jean-Noël Barrot serves as France's digital minister, a key political figure involved in the discourse on AI regulation and autonomy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1165227899625387967696e9c99c63bc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCIENTIFIC PANEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Scientific Panel represents a group of independent experts appointed to advise on the oversight of advanced AI models, a component of the AI regulation framework."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1165227899625387967696e9c99c63bc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MISTRAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mistral is a French AI startup mentioned in the context of the AI rules agreement, potentially affected by the tiered rules for foundational models/GPAIs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1165227899625387967696e9c99c63bc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIGITAL MINISTER'S OFFICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Digital Minister's Office in France is responsible for responding to and analyzing the AI rules agreement, representing France's governmental stance on the issue."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1165227899625387967696e9c99c63bc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COUNCIL'S PRESS RELEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Council's Press Release is an official communication detailing the progress and implications of the AI rules agreement, relevant to the legislative process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1165227899625387967696e9c99c63bc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIVIL SOCIETY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Civil Society refers to groups and organizations outside of government and business that are concerned with how AI regulation might impact society at large, commenting on the proposed rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1165227899625387967696e9c99c63bc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EUROPEAN VALUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"European Values encompass the principles and ethics that guide the EU's approach to AI regulation, emphasizing respect for fundamental rights and strategic self-reliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1165227899625387967696e9c99c63bc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRATEGIC AUTONOMY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Strategic Autonomy relates to the EU's goal of maintaining control over its technological future, including AI, while avoiding over-reliance on external powers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1165227899625387967696e9c99c63bc</data>
</node>
