  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLEAN ENERGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MISSION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clean Energy is the subject of significant commitments and is regarded as inevitable for addressing global electricity needs, highlighting a mission towards sustainability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENEWABLE AND NUCLEAR ENERGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renewable and Nuclear Energy are identified as the main sources of new global electricity supply, representing a shift in technology for energy production.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COAL, OIL, AND GAS DEMAND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The concept of Coal, Oil, and Gas Demand is addressed, with the expectation that their demand will peak in the current decade, indicating a shift towards cleaner energy sources."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORE THAN 100 COUNTRIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"More than 100 countries represent a collective international effort in committing to triple renewable energy capacity by 2030.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;US AND CHINA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The US and China are major greenhouse gas polluters that have committed to collaborative efforts in transitioning towards clean energy.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GLOBAL ENERGY TRANSITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Global Energy Transition is an event that encapsulates the worldwide shift from fossil fuels to renewable and nuclear energy, representing a significant environmental and economic change."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOSSIL FUEL PEAK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fossil Fuel Peak refers to the anticipated peak in demand for coal, oil, and gas, suggesting a declining reliance on these traditional energy sources."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HURRICANE AND WILDFIRE SEASONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hurricane and Wildfire Seasons are environmental events exacerbated by climate change, making this a critical area of concern in discussions about global energy and climate policies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DROUGHT-VULNERABLE PLACES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Drought-Vulnerable Places refers to geographical locations highly susceptible to drought, which are affected by climate change and are a focus of the global energy discussion due to the need for sustainable solutions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITIES FACED WITH RISING TIDES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Communities Faced with Rising Tides are locations affected by sea-level rise, a direct consequence of climate change, relevant to the energy and infrastructure planning.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GLOBAL COMMITMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Global Commitments refer to the pledges made by countries, including more than 100 nations, towards clean energy objectives, marking a pivotal moment in international climate and energy policy.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab9ef562833e5a7fdf735d362fcd67cd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAYE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Daye is a UK-based startup specializing in gynaecological health, offering tampon-based STI screening and other health services, expanding its mission to include STI testing among home screening services."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daye is a startup offering at-home STI testing and vaginal microbiome screening services, aiming to destigmatize sexual health and educate on testing cadence."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dac75c6c1911f180409107d5985483d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VALENTINA MILANOVA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Valentina Milanova is the founder of Daye, with a mission to expand tampon-based screening techniques for broader health utility and convenience."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STI DIAGNOSTIC TAMPON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"STI Diagnostic Tampon is a tampon impregnated with an extraction solution, used for collecting vaginal fluid to test for sexually transmitted infections via PCR technology."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION (PCR)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PCR is a gold standard method used by Daye for testing, identifying the presence of specific pathogens responsible for STIs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHLAMYDIA&quot;, &quot;GONORRHOEA&quot;, &quot;TRICHOMONAS&quot;, &quot;MYCOPLASMA&quot;, &quot;UREAPLASMA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are the five STIs initially included in Daye's tampon-based screening service, representing the focus of the startup's health screening initiative."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GBS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"GBS, a bacteria linked to neonatal infections, is indicated as another screening test Daye plans to offer in the future, emphasizing its health importance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PCR TESTING IN CLINICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PCR testing is a familiar technology, enhanced by its application in Daye's service for STI screening, differentiating it from clinical testing protocols."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEXUAL HEALTH CLINICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sexual health clinics are mentioned as a standard point of reference for STI testing, against which Daye's at-home testing service is being compared."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIV SCREENING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HIV Screening is a health service that patients may forgo due to the convenience of at-home testing offered by Daye."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIV screening is highlighted as a standard procedure in clinics, which could be impacted by the introduction of at-home testing services like Daye's."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dac75c6c1911f180409107d5985483d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IN-CLINIC APPOINTMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"In-clinic appointments are suggested as an alternative by Daye to ensure HIV screening, addressing the concern of clinics' role in comprehensive testing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEALTHCARE OFFERING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Healthcare offering refers to the range of services provided by Daye, including PCR testing and attention to sexual health, framed within the context of healthcare innovation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATIENT SUPPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Patient support encompasses the follow-up services Daye is considering, such as in-clinic HIV screening appointments and consultations, reflecting on the holistic care approach to patients."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45ebf9277a77708b70277514d34175bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLINICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clinics are traditional settings for health information and testing, where patients might be nudged to undergo more comprehensive sexual health checks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dac75c6c1911f180409107d5985483d4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AT-HOME TESTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"At-Home Testing is the method provided by Daye that enables patients to test for STIs privately and conveniently."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dac75c6c1911f180409107d5985483d4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEXUAL HEALTH WORRIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sexual Health Worries refer to concerns related to sexual health that patients might face, which are being addressed by Daye's at-home testing services."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dac75c6c1911f180409107d5985483d4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STIGMATIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stigmatization is an issue Daye aims to mitigate by offering discreet and convenient at-home testing, contributing to a destigmatized approach to sexual health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dac75c6c1911f180409107d5985483d4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESTIGMATIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Destigmatization is the broader goal of Daye's approach to sexual health, where privacy and convenience are provided to encourage testing and education."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dac75c6c1911f180409107d5985483d4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TESTING CADENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Testing Cadence is the recommended frequency of health screenings that Daye emphasizes, which is critical for early detection and management of health concerns."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dac75c6c1911f180409107d5985483d4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POWER MINISTRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Power Ministry is an organization responsible for scheduling tenders for renewable energy capacity to achieve a target of 500 GW of non-fossil fuel power."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-070d69d876b74a5253d91b49175099da</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NTPC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"NTPC is a Power Utility Company, a PSU thermal major that is well-positioned to capture the themes of energy transition and energy security, by planning to add renewable and thermal-based capacities."&lt;SEP&gt;"NTPC is a public sector company planning to add thermal-based capacity as part of its energy security and monetizing its renewable energy arm through an IPO instead of a strategic partnership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-070d69d876b74a5253d91b49175099da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4c3bdf32d2224f3c60e4eca36f5cb82</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVENUE FROM THERMAL-BASED GENERATING STATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BUSINESS_CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Revenue from thermal-based generating stations is a major source of income for NTPC, which operates under long-term power purchase agreements and ensures a return on equity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-070d69d876b74a5253d91b49175099da</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENEWABLE ENERGY CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renewable Energy Capacity refers to the planned increase in NTPC's installed power generation from 3.3 GW to 130 GW, including 60 GW from renewable sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Renewable energy capacity increase is a significant event for NTPC, which plans to scale up to 130 GW, including 60 GW from renewable sources."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-070d69d876b74a5253d91b49175099da</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANT AVAILABILITY FACTOR (PAF)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BUSINESS_CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PAF is a key performance indicator for NTPC's thermal-based stations, reflecting their operational availability and reliability. A PAF of 93.32% in H1FY24 shows an improvement from the previous year and surpasses the normative level."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-070d69d876b74a5253d91b49175099da</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANT LOAD FACTOR (PLF)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BUSINESS_CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PLF is an indicator of NTPC's capacity utilization, with a PLF of 76.62% in H1FY24 showing efficiency in power generation relative to the national average."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-070d69d876b74a5253d91b49175099da</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAPITAL EXPENDITURE (CAPEX)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BUSINESS_CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Capex of ₹28,373 crore for FY24 is indicative of NTPC's investment in infrastructure and expansion, planned for FY25 and FY26, to support its capacity increase and operational enhancements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-070d69d876b74a5253d91b49175099da</data>
</node>
